}0 & 5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6 & -2 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${x}_{32}$, we remove the $3$rd row and $2$nd column: \n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & ∗ & 2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & ∗ & 2 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 6 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ -6 & ∗ & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{32}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${x}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}{M}_{32} \\\\  & =-{M}_{32} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a2272371-24d5-5f31-83e4-a4207fd7fa8d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a2272371-24d5-5f31-83e4-a4207fd7fa8d" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2272371-24d5-5f31-83e4-a4207fd7fa8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c32a0d09-0b2d-5a3b-9258-984ea01ca297" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d4adf8be-5589-54a4-9376-a8eed3ab727e" "answer-c32a0d09-0b2d-5a3b-9258-984ea01ca297" "answer-8d105c7c-f6d4-5e71-9c7c-4dc0c9b642d8" "answer-5ac68f12-2312-545a-8955-97b0d65f236d" "answer-c4808a90-10c0-5c25-923b-83c194b3406e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4adf8be-5589-54a4-9376-a8eed3ab727e" :answer/id #uuid "d4adf8be-5589-54a4-9376-a8eed3ab727e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c32a0d09-0b2d-5a3b-9258-984ea01ca297" :answer/id #uuid "c32a0d09-0b2d-5a3b-9258-984ea01ca297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d105c7c-f6d4-5e71-9c7c-4dc0c9b642d8" :answer/id #uuid "8d105c7c-f6d4-5e71-9c7c-4dc0c9b642d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 6 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ac68f12-2312-545a-8955-97b0d65f236d" :answer/id #uuid "5ac68f12-2312-545a-8955-97b0d65f236d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4808a90-10c0-5c25-923b-83c194b3406e" :answer/id #uuid "c4808a90-10c0-5c25-923b-83c194b3406e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 6 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119783 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d888b8b4-33e2-5465-96a7-f2cf43e527f2" "question-5f805a2f-454d-5b6b-b94e-f4a78a778d84"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d888b8b4-33e2-5465-96a7-f2cf43e527f2" :question/id #uuid "d888b8b4-33e2-5465-96a7-f2cf43e527f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-32746" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$W=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(W) & ={w}_{11}{C}_{11}+{w}_{12}{C}_{12}+{w}_{13}{C}_{13}+{w}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+5\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & ={C}_{11}+5{C}_{13} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ & 5 & ∗ \\\\ 2 & 0 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & ∗ & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+5\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+5\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+5(2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\  & =10(3\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-60\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cfe34648-d2b0-538a-b862-47f017b7fd97"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cfe34648-d2b0-538a-b862-47f017b7fd97" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfe34648-d2b0-538a-b862-47f017b7fd97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-460aef30-08cb-5a20-8328-3ae1a8f946cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1597bd3-5f9c-5dd4-9a8d-382a63c04f0f" "answer-f7b70f72-82d4-57c3-b86c-4d54f9b46376" "answer-460aef30-08cb-5a20-8328-3ae1a8f946cb" "answer-929a7047-4cab-559a-b902-fb43e8ec1d1d" "answer-1c409eaf-a88b-52d0-93e4-e06a7fbd8275"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1597bd3-5f9c-5dd4-9a8d-382a63c04f0f" :answer/id #uuid "e1597bd3-5f9c-5dd4-9a8d-382a63c04f0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7b70f72-82d4-57c3-b86c-4d54f9b46376" :answer/id #uuid "f7b70f72-82d4-57c3-b86c-4d54f9b46376" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-460aef30-08cb-5a20-8328-3ae1a8f946cb" :answer/id #uuid "460aef30-08cb-5a20-8328-3ae1a8f946cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-929a7047-4cab-559a-b902-fb43e8ec1d1d" :answer/id #uuid "929a7047-4cab-559a-b902-fb43e8ec1d1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c409eaf-a88b-52d0-93e4-e06a7fbd8275" :answer/id #uuid "1c409eaf-a88b-52d0-93e4-e06a7fbd8275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f805a2f-454d-5b6b-b94e-f4a78a778d84" :question/id #uuid "5f805a2f-454d-5b6b-b94e-f4a78a778d84" :question/math-academy-id "q-131099" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$T=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -25\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & ={t}_{11}{C}_{11}+{t}_{12}{C}_{12}+{t}_{13}{C}_{13}+{t}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}-10\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =-10{C}_{14} \\\\  & =-10\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & -10 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & ∗\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-10(-1)^{1+4}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =10(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\  & =10(0-4(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)+0) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-40\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2984758c-d2d0-5408-9558-da3f2d0bbdb7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2984758c-d2d0-5408-9558-da3f2d0bbdb7" :answer-field/id #uuid "2984758c-d2d0-5408-9558-da3f2d0bbdb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7df978ee-1cba-5e6d-a0df-7a5d2c0faa72" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7df978ee-1cba-5e6d-a0df-7a5d2c0faa72" "answer-3b6bd69d-eb28-52f2-9e31-c5b78c1f5326" "answer-fd9e80fa-761b-575b-8358-1633af610880" "answer-b58b8460-eabb-5831-9222-ae5190c87747" "answer-e4b666c4-2e1e-5e88-95b7-208ffe3d3b53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7df978ee-1cba-5e6d-a0df-7a5d2c0faa72" :answer/id #uuid "7df978ee-1cba-5e6d-a0df-7a5d2c0faa72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b6bd69d-eb28-52f2-9e31-c5b78c1f5326" :answer/id #uuid "3b6bd69d-eb28-52f2-9e31-c5b78c1f5326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd9e80fa-761b-575b-8358-1633af610880" :answer/id #uuid "fd9e80fa-761b-575b-8358-1633af610880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b58b8460-eabb-5831-9222-ae5190c87747" :answer/id #uuid "b58b8460-eabb-5831-9222-ae5190c87747" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4b666c4-2e1e-5e88-95b7-208ffe3d3b53" :answer/id #uuid "e4b666c4-2e1e-5e88-95b7-208ffe3d3b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119991 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096643 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-47914265-044d-5f89-bb50-8eabdded7a08" "question-b5fdbf2c-dec8-5273-bdaa-1e13a6c2ba92" "question-9347b09d-cd71-571e-b9c7-6616a5a13bf0" "question-b1c67635-2334-5362-a331-e8281f5f234e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-47914265-044d-5f89-bb50-8eabdded7a08" :question/id #uuid "47914265-044d-5f89-bb50-8eabdded7a08" :question/math-academy-id "q-316898" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a67039e1192670e638fbaf88814a6474c9262dee32117d4cdb48db0f0d904fb.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $a$ is perpendicular to $b$, $|a|=12$ and $|b|=9.$ Find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a right triangle. So, we can use Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={12}^{2}+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =144+81 \\\\  & =225\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{225}=15.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eaaafb85-4fd1-52eb-a622-74ba4be6a38d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eaaafb85-4fd1-52eb-a622-74ba4be6a38d" :answer-field/id #uuid "eaaafb85-4fd1-52eb-a622-74ba4be6a38d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-aaa42a66-fbd7-53ab-a6bd-9c97d8cc6552" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aaa42a66-fbd7-53ab-a6bd-9c97d8cc6552"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aaa42a66-fbd7-53ab-a6bd-9c97d8cc6552" :answer/id #uuid "aaa42a66-fbd7-53ab-a6bd-9c97d8cc6552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b5fdbf2c-dec8-5273-bdaa-1e13a6c2ba92" :question/id #uuid "b5fdbf2c-dec8-5273-bdaa-1e13a6c2ba92" :question/math-academy-id "q-316812" :question/problem "![](images/08/08ac5be11bc156cf1e43fc7d5e6283b4c4514c78d3280180f8d66eca8c66eab6.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $a$ is perpendicular to $b$, $|a|=4$ and $|b|=7.$ Find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a right triangle. So, we can use Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+{7}^{2} \\\\  & =65\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{65}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6efd4c2e-cb0c-5f1d-89f9-33793724f1d1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6efd4c2e-cb0c-5f1d-89f9-33793724f1d1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6efd4c2e-cb0c-5f1d-89f9-33793724f1d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-10762df6-57f0-5b84-885e-274abb0ee789" :answer-field/choices ["answer-10762df6-57f0-5b84-885e-274abb0ee789"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10762df6-57f0-5b84-885e-274abb0ee789" :answer/id #uuid "10762df6-57f0-5b84-885e-274abb0ee789" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{65}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9347b09d-cd71-571e-b9c7-6616a5a13bf0" :question/id #uuid "9347b09d-cd71-571e-b9c7-6616a5a13bf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-118912" :question/problem "In rectangle $ABCD$, $AB=18$ and $BC=9.$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/3e/3e03c8d3377aef27d7542ef2d734ebd64d00bbc1539e63222b7df9abc696bd44.png)\n\nAs we can see from the picture above, in $△BAD$ we have $∠BAD={90}^{∘}$, $AB=18$ and $AD=BC=9.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{BD}| & =BD \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}+A{D}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{18}^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{405} \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|=9\\sqrt{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-884db0bd-f9ab-5fb9-9f2d-26d5107b8c4a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-884db0bd-f9ab-5fb9-9f2d-26d5107b8c4a" :answer-field/id #uuid "884db0bd-f9ab-5fb9-9f2d-26d5107b8c4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bfa0a12f-cda8-5fd5-abe7-5e30e71cce8e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e3d71863-c6cb-51c1-9392-5d2245d50ab7" "answer-d4e0b7d3-574e-5e58-ac51-e9d34b36fed0" "answer-c932bcf2-cafc-5b21-8eb5-b04c461de955" "answer-750024aa-db50-5f98-8404-f6e69c56d142" "answer-bfa0a12f-cda8-5fd5-abe7-5e30e71cce8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3d71863-c6cb-51c1-9392-5d2245d50ab7" :answer/id #uuid "e3d71863-c6cb-51c1-9392-5d2245d50ab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4e0b7d3-574e-5e58-ac51-e9d34b36fed0" :answer/id #uuid "d4e0b7d3-574e-5e58-ac51-e9d34b36fed0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c932bcf2-cafc-5b21-8eb5-b04c461de955" :answer/id #uuid "c932bcf2-cafc-5b21-8eb5-b04c461de955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-750024aa-db50-5f98-8404-f6e69c56d142" :answer/id #uuid "750024aa-db50-5f98-8404-f6e69c56d142" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfa0a12f-cda8-5fd5-abe7-5e30e71cce8e" :answer/id #uuid "bfa0a12f-cda8-5fd5-abe7-5e30e71cce8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1c67635-2334-5362-a331-e8281f5f234e" :question/id #uuid "b1c67635-2334-5362-a331-e8281f5f234e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316909" :question/problem "In rectangle $ABCD,$ $AB=10$ and $BC=6\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the **exact** value of $|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|.$\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](images/53/537669ec91bb6fd620d64816d4ccf0e0a5c403aa8ba6e03c8fb89c8d71785d24.png)\n\nAs we can see from the picture above, in $△BAD$ we have $m∠BAD={90}^{∘},$ $AB=10,$ and $AD=BC=6\\sqrt{2}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{BD}| & =BD \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}+A{D}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+(6\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+72} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{172} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{43}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|=2\\sqrt{43}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9362a981-d476-5fb3-b9f4-48cf3184521d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9362a981-d476-5fb3-b9f4-48cf3184521d" :answer-field/id #uuid "9362a981-d476-5fb3-b9f4-48cf3184521d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-360a01a5-0fde-5f9a-bcdd-05b77ca562f5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-360a01a5-0fde-5f9a-bcdd-05b77ca562f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-360a01a5-0fde-5f9a-bcdd-05b77ca562f5" :answer/id #uuid "360a01a5-0fde-5f9a-bcdd-05b77ca562f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{43}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097829 :tutorial/content "Suppose we have a vector $\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\textbf{a}.$ We denote its **magnitude**, also known as its *modulus* or *length*, as $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$ or $|\\textbf{a}|.$\n\nFor example, the vector below has a magnitude of $8,$ denoted $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|=8.$\n\n![](images/71/71105c9d5920ec71e61fe1176021024188a86bd8023671b79e0ce89082994299.png)\n\nNow, let's consider the following situation. Suppose that the vector $\\textbf{a}$ is directed vertically upwards and $|\\textbf{a}|=6,$ while $\\textbf{b}$ is directed horizontally to the right and $|\\textbf{b}|=8.$ How can we find $|\\textbf{a}+\\textbf{b}|?$\n\nFirst, we use the triangle law of addition to find the resultant $\\textbf{a}+\\textbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/ff/ffd155d3b72015a72d878fc8089381a5bcf5a97f698f85945642189ea7368a3f.png)\n\nNotice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{a}+\\text{b}{|}^{2} & =|\\text{a}{|}^{2}+|\\text{b}{|}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}+{8}^{2} \\\\  & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\textbf{a}+\\textbf{b}|=\\sqrt{100}=10.\n$$\n\n**Important**: In the above calculation we wrote $|\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}|^2 = |\\mathbf{a}|^2+|\\mathbf{b}|^2$. This works only when the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are at right angles, and the relationship is not true in general. We'll see how to deal with non-right-angled vectors soon." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097839 :tutorial/content "When the triangle law for addition does *not* give a right triangle, we *cannot* use the Pythagorean theorem to compute the magnitude of the sum.\n\nFor example, using the triangle law to draw the sum $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ for the vectors below, we do not get a right triangle. Instead, we get a triangle with an obtuse angle $\\theta.$\n\n![](images/96/967966ec9d8ac0b7358623645de0e7931ef4d6cc87bd919d1f0cf04f7ca6ca28.png)\n\nWe do not obtain a right triangle here, so we cannot use the Pythagorean theorem. However, we can use the law of cosines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2}-2|a||b|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, given any two vectors that form a triangle using the triangle addition law, we can always use the law of cosines to compute the magnitude of the sum." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097805 :tutorial/content "![](images/0a/0ac79071675ca17dbb25708f8131a0f1706c29ffe69c750969112fd6a097d1f6.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $|\\mathbf{a}|=4$ and $|\\mathbf{b}|=5.$ How can we find $|\\mathbf{a+b}|?$ \n\nFirst, we use the triangle law of addition to find $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/dd/dd9b407a04394d9648db4671788791a8cf615b7755c1efead6f637fe26a40562.png)\n\nWe do not obtain a right triangle here, so we cannot use the Pythagorean theorem. But we can use the law of cosines, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2}-2|a||b|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({120}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+{5}^{2}-2\\cdot 4\\cdot 5\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =16+25+20 \\\\  & =61\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|\\mathbf{a+b}|=\\sqrt{61}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096881 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157229 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6630be77-163d-5764-855a-2fae7c91d8ec" "question-56a51414-b2fd-5ffa-892f-1c507337dc45" "question-8a46ff8e-4967-5da0-abf9-a76617f494fb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6630be77-163d-5764-855a-2fae7c91d8ec" :question/id #uuid "6630be77-163d-5764-855a-2fae7c91d8ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-182436" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧¬(A∨B))\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add a column for the part of the expression that's in parentheses, $A∨B:$ \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $¬(A∨B):$ \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nNext, we add the column for $A∧¬(A∨B):$ \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨B)\\,$ | $\\,A∧¬(A∨B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nFinally, we add the column for $¬(A∧¬(A∨B))):$ \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨B)\\,$ | $\\,A∧¬(A∨B)\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧¬(A∨B))\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-efb2eb80-a99a-543d-8a79-fa9a61a2b4a9" "answer-field-4353ba2f-a358-569a-afa6-eb31d9a82c37" "answer-field-0765c