r-field-6a3b405b-c62a-50ce-8f47-28f67b376d14" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a3b405b-c62a-50ce-8f47-28f67b376d14" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-d36048ef-1eaf-5ea7-967f-2db3db3f1b9d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-055977ef-2324-5ea5-bff8-b5ca65af690b" "answer-d36048ef-1eaf-5ea7-967f-2db3db3f1b9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-055977ef-2324-5ea5-bff8-b5ca65af690b" :answer/id #uuid "055977ef-2324-5ea5-bff8-b5ca65af690b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d36048ef-1eaf-5ea7-967f-2db3db3f1b9d" :answer/id #uuid "d36048ef-1eaf-5ea7-967f-2db3db3f1b9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8a46ff8e-4967-5da0-abf9-a76617f494fb" :question/id #uuid "8a46ff8e-4967-5da0-abf9-a76617f494fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-182423" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨B)∧A\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add a column for the part of the expression that's in parentheses, $A∨B:$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for the negation, $¬(A∨B):$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $¬(A∨B)∧A:$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨B)\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨B)∧A\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b636f95a-54e9-5bc6-9d35-99e416c0d542" "answer-field-e1db2ccb-1e09-58dd-b54c-865c50944010" "answer-field-3d50b378-d445-5886-ba7a-be3d024c7869" "answer-field-7cd4ee36-3ecf-55a3-ae3b-35083b25c489"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b636f95a-54e9-5bc6-9d35-99e416c0d542" :answer-field/id #uuid "b636f95a-54e9-5bc6-9d35-99e416c0d542" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-75c3a0cd-5d64-5ba9-be50-94c8339db8e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-75c3a0cd-5d64-5ba9-be50-94c8339db8e5" "answer-0d47e90c-cb67-523a-9838-4a060ea2b1b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75c3a0cd-5d64-5ba9-be50-94c8339db8e5" :answer/id #uuid "75c3a0cd-5d64-5ba9-be50-94c8339db8e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d47e90c-cb67-523a-9838-4a060ea2b1b1" :answer/id #uuid "0d47e90c-cb67-523a-9838-4a060ea2b1b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e1db2ccb-1e09-58dd-b54c-865c50944010" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1db2ccb-1e09-58dd-b54c-865c50944010" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-3194749a-f904-54db-aceb-5793a6f6cc3d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3194749a-f904-54db-aceb-5793a6f6cc3d" "answer-d5aae7e9-8028-5890-a5d9-f928fcbd9d86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3194749a-f904-54db-aceb-5793a6f6cc3d" :answer/id #uuid "3194749a-f904-54db-aceb-5793a6f6cc3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5aae7e9-8028-5890-a5d9-f928fcbd9d86" :answer/id #uuid "d5aae7e9-8028-5890-a5d9-f928fcbd9d86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3d50b378-d445-5886-ba7a-be3d024c7869" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d50b378-d445-5886-ba7a-be3d024c7869" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-2b211de7-f81b-5802-9702-d7fdd227f537" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b211de7-f81b-5802-9702-d7fdd227f537" "answer-3c1c9945-65c8-5090-a448-64744d15b965"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b211de7-f81b-5802-9702-d7fdd227f537" :answer/id #uuid "2b211de7-f81b-5802-9702-d7fdd227f537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c1c9945-65c8-5090-a448-64744d15b965" :answer/id #uuid "3c1c9945-65c8-5090-a448-64744d15b965" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7cd4ee36-3ecf-55a3-ae3b-35083b25c489" :answer-field/id #uuid "7cd4ee36-3ecf-55a3-ae3b-35083b25c489" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-8772135a-e2dd-5640-b042-d52bb6d30e0e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8772135a-e2dd-5640-b042-d52bb6d30e0e" "answer-fcb5f2a4-4d43-5e10-8690-03c6085975db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8772135a-e2dd-5640-b042-d52bb6d30e0e" :answer/id #uuid "8772135a-e2dd-5640-b042-d52bb6d30e0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcb5f2a4-4d43-5e10-8690-03c6085975db" :answer/id #uuid "fcb5f2a4-4d43-5e10-8690-03c6085975db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157230 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8916118b-53b3-5d09-94d6-cc82ce4ab29d" "question-71caea99-6397-53f2-9820-70b75fa92d6e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8916118b-53b3-5d09-94d6-cc82ce4ab29d" :question/id #uuid "8916118b-53b3-5d09-94d6-cc82ce4ab29d" :question/math-academy-id "q-182516" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\n \n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q){{field-4}}Q\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧¬(P\\text{ }∧¬Q) & ≡(\\text{T}∨\\text{T})∧¬(\\text{T}∧¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q) & ≡(\\text{T}∨\\text{F})∧¬(\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q) & ≡(\\text{F}∨\\text{T})∧¬(\\text{F}∧¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)$ is logically equivalent to $Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)≡Q.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f078c0e1-69b9-595c-b1b4-c6f0f24a2b9c" "answer-field-4846790c-0817-50de-86db-9597bb81f429" "answer-field-1562b94f-b92a-51be-82d8-44a0fe8a5bf7" "answer-field-ff5bcb5d-0db3-5161-b056-6df3af0bf4f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f078c0e1-69b9-595c-b1b4-c6f0f24a2b9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "f078c0e1-69b9-595c-b1b4-c6f0f24a2b9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-41967852-735b-559a-887e-ebb02555fee8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d1f5b939-2fc5-50d9-9c87-bf4776c4ea0d" "answer-41967852-735b-559a-887e-ebb02555fee8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1f5b939-2fc5-50d9-9c87-bf4776c4ea0d" :answer/id #uuid "d1f5b939-2fc5-50d9-9c87-bf4776c4ea0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41967852-735b-559a-887e-ebb02555fee8" :answer/id #uuid "41967852-735b-559a-887e-ebb02555fee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4846790c-0817-50de-86db-9597bb81f429" :answer-field/id #uuid "4846790c-0817-50de-86db-9597bb81f429" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c35e7574-b8be-58ca-bde9-d14d5025bb20" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c35e7574-b8be-58ca-bde9-d14d5025bb20" "answer-5c4207c3-5d89-5e1b-a6de-81a689a34ca7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c35e7574-b8be-58ca-bde9-d14d5025bb20" :answer/id #uuid "c35e7574-b8be-58ca-bde9-d14d5025bb20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c4207c3-5d89-5e1b-a6de-81a689a34ca7" :answer/id #uuid "5c4207c3-5d89-5e1b-a6de-81a689a34ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1562b94f-b92a-51be-82d8-44a0fe8a5bf7" :answer-field/id #uuid "1562b94f-b92a-51be-82d8-44a0fe8a5bf7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-38ed73c4-7b08-5bb6-86a4-3da74948ecb3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1843c7c7-429a-52e4-a053-a385556510ee" "answer-38ed73c4-7b08-5bb6-86a4-3da74948ecb3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1843c7c7-429a-52e4-a053-a385556510ee" :answer/id #uuid "1843c7c7-429a-52e4-a053-a385556510ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38ed73c4-7b08-5bb6-86a4-3da74948ecb3" :answer/id #uuid "38ed73c4-7b08-5bb6-86a4-3da74948ecb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ff5bcb5d-0db3-5161-b056-6df3af0bf4f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff5bcb5d-0db3-5161-b056-6df3af0bf4f3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f8cc5ed5-dd56-5bc9-a238-5a2d4adbf7e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f8cc5ed5-dd56-5bc9-a238-5a2d4adbf7e0" "answer-303abb5e-06b3-51da-a1de-660d493740be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8cc5ed5-dd56-5bc9-a238-5a2d4adbf7e0" :answer/id #uuid "f8cc5ed5-dd56-5bc9-a238-5a2d4adbf7e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≡" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-303abb5e-06b3-51da-a1de-660d493740be" :answer/id #uuid "303abb5e-06b3-51da-a1de-660d493740be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≢" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-71caea99-6397-53f2-9820-70b75fa92d6e" :question/id #uuid "71caea99-6397-53f2-9820-70b75fa92d6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-182613" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧(B∨¬A)\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\nA∧(B∨¬A){{field-4}}A∧B\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧(B∨¬A) & ≡\\text{T}∧(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧(\\text{T}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧B & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧(B∨¬A) & ≡\\text{F}∧(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∧(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧(B∨¬A)\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $A∧(B∨¬A)$ is logically equivalent to $A∧B,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.  \n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{F},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nA∧(B∨¬A)≡A∧B.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1fb20fee-89a9-593f-ae68-43e79d19d3dc" "answer-field-5a09a91e-3e45-5d4b-8ffa-16a8fee8c788" "answer-field-77fba244-8d11-51cc-9804-38249758af03" "answer-field-06bdfac5-f17e-59d3-ae6b-119b67476434"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1fb20fee-89a9-593f-ae68-43e79d19d3dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fb20fee-89a9-593f-ae68-43e79d19d3dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-3c1109da-0464-59e7-83cf-b09bfc11f8a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-23c9eba8-49d9-54ce-9555-fd9bfe88983f" "answer-3c1109da-0464-59e7-83cf-b09bfc11f8a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23c9eba8-49d9-54ce-9555-fd9bfe88983f" :answer/id #uuid "23c9eba8-49d9-54ce-9555-fd9bfe88983f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c1109da-0464-59e7-83cf-b09bfc11f8a5" :answer/id #uuid "3c1109da-0464-59e7-83cf-b09bfc11f8a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5a09a91e-3e45-5d4b-8ffa-16a8fee8c788" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a09a91e-3e45-5d4b-8ffa-16a8fee8c788" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-8471d567-27ce-546e-a2e5-136c8dcb2a43" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8471d567-27ce-546e-a2e5-136c8dcb2a43" "answer-c5ebe3a2-9f21-5b57-a32f-24e9ff99f95d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8471d567-27ce-546e-a2e5-136c8dcb2a43" :answer/id #uuid "8471d567-27ce-546e-a2e5-136c8dcb2a43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5ebe3a2-9f21-5b57-a32f-24e9ff99f95d" :answer/id #uuid "c5ebe3a2-9f21-5b57-a32f-24e9ff99f95d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-77fba244-8d11-51cc-9804-38249758af03" :answer-field/id #uuid "77fba244-8d11-51cc-9804-38249758af03" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-93f34d1e-65d5-5786-912e-688d68306a1a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-93f34d1e-65d5-5786-912e-688d68306a1a" "answer-1463f092-5e79-543b-8ea1-36ea96372e72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93f34d1e-65d5-5786-912e-688d68306a1a" :answer/id #uuid "93f34d1e-65d5-5786-912e-688d68306a1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1463f092-5e79-543b-8ea1-36ea96372e72" :answer/id #uuid "1463f092-5e79-543b-8ea1-36ea96372e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06bdfac5-f17e-59d3-ae6b-119b67476434" :answer-field/id #uuid "06bdfac5-f17e-59d3-ae6b-119b67476434" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-720ca6ed-930d-58f4-8d95-c74d402954f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-720ca6ed-930d-58f4-8d95-c74d402954f8" "answer-10b790e6-bfc7-5680-adfc-00f8a8ce7b5d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-720ca6ed-930d-58f4-8d95-c74d402954f8" :answer/id #uuid "720ca6ed-930d-58f4-8d95-c74d402954f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≡" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10b790e6-bfc7-5680-adfc-00f8a8ce7b5d" :answer/id #uuid "10b790e6-bfc7-5680-adfc-00f8a8ce7b5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≢" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-149a9180-216e-5fde-a636-2e26041dbcaf" "question-60ece590-e8a6-5abb-9e47-471816aaf089"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-149a9180-216e-5fde-a636-2e26041dbcaf" :question/id #uuid "149a9180-216e-5fde-a636-2e26041dbcaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-127970" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nI. $¬P∨(P∧¬Q)$\n\nII. $¬P∨Q$\n\nIII. $¬P∨¬Q$" :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨(P∧¬Q)\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬P∨(P∧¬Q)$ and $¬P∨¬Q$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d014b9ff-a538-5081-af17-3c58ef8605eb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d014b9ff-a538-5081-af17-3c58ef8605eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "d014b9ff-a538-5081-af17-3c58ef8605eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-82f488ba-2af6-5a11-9c9c-28b885bd3a16" :answer-field/choices ["answer-af654f30-cbc6-5e4e-b60e-f0592efb2afa" "answer-82f488ba-2af6-5a11-9c9c-28b885bd3a16" "answer-1569c631-3e1c-545e-bca8-4b339bbf907d" "answer-26c6b578-4875-5aa4-8f07-11014a12692d" "answer-00dfcdf9-ccb2-5f6c-a192-151925743c47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af654f30-cbc6-5e4e-b60e-f0592efb2afa" :answer/id #uuid "af654f30-cbc6-5e4e-b60e-f0592efb2afa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82f488ba-2af6-5a11-9c9c-28b885bd3a16" :answer/id #uuid "82f488ba-2af6-5a11-9c9c-28b885bd3a16" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1569c631-3e1c-545e-bca8-4b339bbf907d" :answer/id #uuid "1569c631-3e1c-545e-bca8-4b339bbf907d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26c6b578-4875-5aa4-8f07-11014a12692d" :answer/id #uuid "26c6b578-4875-5aa4-8f07-11014a12692d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00dfcdf9-ccb2-5f6c-a192-151925743c47" :answer/id #uuid "00dfcdf9-ccb2-5f6c-a192-151925743c47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-60ece590-e8a6-5abb-9e47-471816aaf089" :question/id #uuid "60ece590-e8a6-5abb-9e47-471816aaf089" :question/math-academy-id "q-127961" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nI. $¬(A∨B)$\n\nII. $A∨¬B$\n\nIII. $¬(A∧B)$" :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨B)\\,$ | $\\,A∨¬B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that none of the statements have the same truth table, so none of them are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-47faa176-79c4-52dc-b052-4e8bdcb68270"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-47faa176-79c4-52dc-b052-4e8bdcb68270" :answer-field/id #uuid "47faa176-79c4-52dc-b052-4e8bdcb68270" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-85c9254d-fa16-53ba-8824-4e1914265d1f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4147f9fb-3cf6-5c90-9091-5db61b63fab1" "answer-0d16d097-d7aa-5ffe-bee2-48e3a453468b" "answer-e2884a12-3356-5c32-a805-fd39f121224d" "answer-c3928ceb-899c-5b8d-9495-f4c446ac0b05" "answer-85c9254d-fa16-53ba-8824-4e1914265d1f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4147f9fb-3cf6-5c90-9091-5db61b63fab1" :answer/id #uuid "4147f9fb-3cf6-5c90-9091-5db61b63fab1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d16d097-d7aa-5ffe-bee2-48e3a453468b" :answer/id #uuid "0d16d097-d7aa-5ffe-bee2-48e3a453468b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2884a12-3356-5c32-a805-fd39f121224d" :answer/id #uuid "e2884a12-3356-5c32-a805-fd39f121224d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3928ceb-899c-5b8d-9495-f4c446ac0b05" :answer/id #uuid "c3928ceb-899c-5b8d-9495-f4c446ac0b05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85c9254d-fa16-53ba-8824-4e1914265d1f" :answer/id #uuid "85c9254d-fa16-53ba-8824-4e1914265d1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158579 :tutorial/content "Two statements are **logically equivalent** if they have identical truth values in their respective truth tables. In this lesson, we'll use truth tables to show that two complex compound statements are logically equivalent. \n\nIf two statements $P$ and $Q$ are logically equivalent, we write\n\n$$\nP\\equiv Q\n$$\n\nwhere the symbol \"$\\equiv$\" means \"is logically equivalent to.\"\n\nFor example, let's use a truth table to prove the following logical equivalence:\n\n$$\n(A \\land \\neg A) \\lor B \\equiv B\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct truth tables with columns $A$ and $B$ containing all possible combinations of truth values. Then, we create another column for $\\neg A,$ which has the opposite truth values to $A.$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $A \\land \\neg A.$ Recall that $A\\land \\neg A$ is true if $A$ is true and $\\neg A$ is true and is false otherwise. In this case, $A\\land \\neg A$ is always false.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\,$ | $\\, A \\land \\neg A \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n\nFinally, we complete the table with a column for $(A \\land \\neg A) \\lor B.$ Recall that $(A \\land \\neg A) \\lor B$ is true if $(A \\land \\neg A)$ is true, or $B$ is true, or both are true. \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\,$ | $\\, A \\land \\neg A \\,$ | $\\, (A \\land \\neg A) \\lor B \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n\nWe see that the truth values of $(A \\land \\neg A) \\lor B$ are the same as the truth values of $B.$ This proves that $(A \\land \\neg A) \\lor B$ is logically equivalent to $B.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157478 :activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105770 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e4e6ce71-c74f-5790-9b61-f458926b26f7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e4e6ce71-c74f-5790-9b61-f458926b26f7" :question/id #uuid "e4e6ce71-c74f-5790-9b61-f458926b26f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-18236" :question/problem "The eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3k+1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-k$ is  $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3k+1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =-k\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3k+16\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-k \\\\ -5k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2 &=-k, \\\\ 3k+16 &=-5k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n2=-k\\,⟹\\,k=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $k=-2$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k+16 & =-5k \\\\ 3\\cdot (-2)+16 & =-5\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 10 & =10,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a true statement.\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e3ef38cb-d22b-5c07-9abf-231f5e6be217"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e3ef38cb-d22b-5c07-9abf-231f5e6be217" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3ef38cb-d22b-5c07-9abf-231f5e6be217" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8be08705-3f7e-5fdb-a167-e4244e9ea1fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8be08705-3f7e-5fdb-a167-e4244e9ea1fd" "answer-f462c8dd-3f8b-5230-9dc9-c062aa74de47" "answer-37563492-e7cf-5fdf-9ea2-b0e40fe05275" "answer-07eb1dc5-98f3-5daa-91e3-a9e09abb0895" "answer-e4291a8f-63e2-5130-a4f3-66c8b39bc724"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8be08705-3f7e-5fdb-a167-e4244e9ea1fd" :answer/id #uuid "8be08705-3f7e-5fdb-a167-e4244e9ea1fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f462c8dd-3f8b-5230-9dc9-c062aa74de47" :answer/id #uuid "f462c8dd-3f8b-5230-9dc9-c062aa74de47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37563492-e7cf-5fdf-9ea2-b0e40fe05275" :answer/id #uuid "37563492-e7cf-5fdf-9ea2-b0e40fe05275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07eb1dc5-98f3-5daa-91e3-a9e09abb0895" :answer/id #uuid "07eb1dc5-98f3-5daa-91e3-a9e09abb0895" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4291a8f-63e2-5130-a4f3-66c8b39bc724" :answer/id #uuid "e4291a8f-63e2-5130-a4f3-66c8b39bc724" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105769 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-48224f9c-af15-5271-930c-05fc20cc3fbf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-48224f9c-af15-5271-930c-05fc20cc3fbf" :question/id #uuid "48224f9c-af15-5271-930c-05fc20cc3fbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-107312" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $v$ is an eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{3}$ then $v$ is also an eigenvector of the matrix ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to $\\lambda =4.$\n\nII. An eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2$ is also an eigenvector of the inverse ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nIII. If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3,$ then $5v$ is also an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =15.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement is false. By the definition of an eigenvector, we have \n\n$$\nAv=\\frac{1}{3}v.\n$$\n\n \nMultiplying it by ${A}^{-1}$ from the left, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=\\frac{1}{3}{A}^{-1}v.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $3$, we get \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}v=3v.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $v$ is an eigenvector of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $3.$\n\n**Note:** In general, an eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to an eigenvalue $\\lambda$ is an eigenvector of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.$\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the statement above, an eigenvector of $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2$ is an eigenvector of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(5v) &=5Av=5(3v)=3(5v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(5v)=3(5v),$ and $5v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $5v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =3.$\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d76769ca-539d-5bea-bc37-7af743caadc7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d76769ca-539d-5bea-bc37-7af743caadc7" :answer-field/id #uuid "d76769ca-539d-5bea-bc37-7af743caadc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e2c9af5a-45a8-5973-9c44-186d59bb5f68" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4537924c-6e29-55ff-b3f8-dc181ec0e42f" "answer-bd39d6f9-1a79-5269-bb60-a3705107fe12" "answer-e2c9af5a-45a8-5973-9c44-186d59bb5f68" "answer-ba493e6d-d0cf-5095-bfa8-8805ceb595dc" "answer-b0aecb63-c63a-50f2-a367-8c0bc46f3d0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4537924c-6e29-55ff-b3f8-dc181ec0e42f" :answer/id #uuid "4537924c-6e29-55ff-b3f8-dc181ec0e42f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd39d6f9-1a79-5269-bb60-a3705107fe12" :answer/id #uuid "bd39d6f9-1a79-5269-bb60-a3705107fe12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2c9af5a-45a8-5973-9c44-186d59bb5f68" :answer/id #uuid "e2c9af5a-45a8-5973-9c44-186d59bb5f68" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba493e6d-d0cf-5095-bfa8-8805ceb595dc" :answer/id #uuid "ba493e6d-d0cf-5095-bfa8-8805ceb595dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0aecb63-c63a-50f2-a367-8c0bc46f3d0d" :answer/id #uuid "b0aecb63-c63a-50f2-a367-8c0bc46f3d0d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-29b930e0-d300-5c18-b22e-b6c8fa5110b7" :activity/id #uuid "29b930e0-d300-5c18-b22e-b6c8fa5110b7" :activity/title "The Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of a 2x2 Matrix" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048819 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-5e138194-7714-5b10-b6fc-e0340f52b114" "step-e4278250-85d4-5e96-add4-c7d4c1187239" "step-7931e841-3cfd-560d-84bf-f26f00e03321" "step-f02310af-9ad3-5d7c-90ac-a5a1f4308abf" "step-3ceb3caa-5108-55c6-93e3-8d37c4a57f4a"] :activity/first-step "step-5e138194-7714-5b10-b6fc-e0340f52b114" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5e138194-7714-5b10-b6fc-e0340f52b114" :step/id #uuid "5e138194-7714-5b10-b6fc-e0340f52b114" :step/content 17592186287815 :step/next "step-e4278250-85d4-5e96-add4-c7d4c1187239" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e4278250-85d4-5e96-add4-c7d4c1187239" :step/id #uuid "e4278250-85d4-5e96-add4-c7d4c1187239" :step/content "question-e4e6ce71-c74f-5790-9b61-f458926b26f7" :step/next "step-7931e841-3cfd-560d-84bf-f26f00e03321" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7931e841-3cfd-560d-84bf-f26f00e03321" :step/id #uuid "7931e841-3cfd-560d-84bf-f26f00e03321" :step/content 17592186345124 :step/next "step-f02310af-9ad3-5d7c-90ac-a5a1f4308abf" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f02310af-9ad3-5d7c-90ac-a5a1f4308abf" :step/id #uuid "f02310af-9ad3-5d7c-90ac-a5a1f4308abf" :step/content 17592186369010 :step/next "step-3ceb3caa-5108-55c6-93e3-8d37c4a57f4a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3ceb3caa-5108-55c6-93e3-8d37c4a57f4a" :step/id #uuid "3ceb3caa-5108-55c6-93e3-8d37c4a57f4a" :step/content "question-48224f9c-af15-5271-930c-05fc20cc3fbf" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138432 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6bd84e69-7c5f-5a4e-bce4-f665a1006214" "question-52c4a416-f053-5e55-99b6-12fd0ef1b322" "question-493093e8-547a-52cb-ae1e-43635271726b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6bd84e69-7c5f-5a4e-bce4-f665a1006214" :question/id #uuid "6bd84e69-7c5f-5a4e-bce4-f665a1006214" :question/math-academy-id "q-52005" :question/problem "The distance $d$, in meters, a falling body travels after being released from rest varies directly with the **square** of the time $t,$ measured in seconds, since the body was released. If the body covers $12$ meters in $2$ seconds, then what is the constant of variation?" :question/worked-solution "The distance $d$ is directly proportional to the square of the time $t$, so we have\n\n$$\nd=k{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the constant of variation.\n\nWe are told that $d=12\\,\\text{m}$ when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$ We can use this information to solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =k\\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\ 12 & =k\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\frac{12}{4} & =k \\\\ 3 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of variation is $k=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cf2bf7fa-473d-5f46-831b-f02037509aa6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cf2bf7fa-473d-5f46-831b-f02037509aa6" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf2bf7fa-473d-5f46-831b-f02037509aa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d611d837-c607-55f1-84f6-82a363b4fcc6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d611d837-c607-55f1-84f6-82a363b4fcc6" "answer-1897ea72-c13e-5fd4-8083-32c921ead598" "answer-82b7408e-0165-58fb-9ffe-29dd90fb32bb" "answer-4786e8d1-90b1-5d13-9ebd-a4ddaedea0e0" "answer-58ba7898-216c-5d88-b22b-f355ac55120b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d611d837-c607-55f1-84f6-82a363b4fcc6" :answer/id #uuid "d611d837-c607-55f1-84f6-82a363b4fcc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1897ea72-c13e-5fd4-8083-32c921ead598" :answer/id #uuid "1897ea72-c13e-5fd4-8083-32c921ead598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82b7408e-0165-58fb-9ffe-29dd90fb32bb" :answer/id #uuid "82b7408e-0165-58fb-9ffe-29dd90fb32bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4786e8d1-90b1-5d13-9ebd-a4ddaedea0e0" :answer/id #uuid "4786e8d1-90b1-5d13-9ebd-a4ddaedea0e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58ba7898-216c-5d88-b22b-f355ac55120b" :answer/id #uuid "58ba7898-216c-5d88-b22b-f355ac55120b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-52c4a416-f053-5e55-99b6-12fd0ef1b322" :question/id #uuid "52c4a416-f053-5e55-99b6-12fd0ef1b322" :question/math-academy-id "q-120299" :question/problem "The surface $S,$ in square centimeters, of a cylinder whose height equals the radius of its base varies directly with the **square** of its radius $r,$ measured in centimeters. If the surface is $16\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}$ when the radius is $2\\,\\text{cm},$ then what is the constant of variation?" :question/worked-solution "The surface $S$ is directly proportional to the radius $r,$ so we have\n\n$$\nS=k{r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the constant of variation.\n\nWe are told that $S=16\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}$ when $r=2\\,\\text{cm}.$ We can use this information to solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16\\pi  & =k\\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\ 16\\pi  & =k\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\frac{16\\pi }{4} & =k \\\\ 4\\pi  & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of variation is $k=4\\pi .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4782ff3c-c734-5dad-88e3-9bed03473528"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4782ff3c-c734-5dad-88e3-9bed03473528" :answer-field/id #uuid "4782ff3c-c734-5dad-88e3-9bed03473528" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-34146648-0aef-5194-b0bd-b28640147dea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0b0f61ca-4b31-5d02-b3fa-da62506bb922" "answer-34146648-0aef-5194-b0bd-b28640147dea" "answer-31844f5d-e1c6-58a5-911d-752c2c6738db" "answer-4841b2db-6473-515a-b60c-cb4143294f92" "answer-178a11f1-2e2f-512c-81ef-7ba747eb04b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b0f61ca-4b31-5d02-b3fa-da62506bb922" :answer/id #uuid "0b0f61ca-4b31-5d02-b3fa-da62506bb922" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34146648-0aef-5194-b0bd-b28640147dea" :answer/id #uuid "34146648-0aef-5194-b0bd-b28640147dea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31844f5d-e1c6-58a5-911d-752c2c6738db" :answer/id #uuid "31844f5d-e1c6-58a5-911d-752c2c6738db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4841b2db-6473-515a-b60c-cb4143294f92" :answer/id #uuid "4841b2db-6473-515a-b60c-cb4143294f92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-178a11f1-2e2f-512c-81ef-7ba747eb04b5" :answer/id #uuid "178a11f1-2e2f-512c-81ef-7ba747eb04b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-493093e8-547a-52cb-ae1e-43635271726b" :question/id #uuid "493093e8-547a-52cb-ae1e-43635271726b" :question/math-academy-id "q-210542" :question/problem "The electrostatic force $F,$ in newtons ($N$), exerted between two identical charged particles kept at a fixed distance apart, varies directly with the **square** of the charge $q$ of each particle, measured in coulombs $(C).$ If the electrostatic force is $8\\,976\\,N$ when the charges are $2\\,C,$ then express $F$ in terms of $q.$\n\n$F=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The electrostatic force $F$ is directly proportional to the square of the charge $q,$ so we have\n\n$$\nF=k{q}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the constant of variation.\n\nWe are told that $F=8\\,976\\,\\text{N}$ when $q=2\\,\\text{C}.$ We can use this information to solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\,976 & =k\\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\ 8\\,976 & =k\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\frac{8\\,976}{4} & =k \\\\ 2\\,244 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our direct variation equation is\n\n$$\nF=2\\,244{q}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d70374a3-fd1e-563a-bc82-ef9476203959"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d70374a3-fd1e-563a-bc82-ef9476203959" :answer-field/id #uuid "d70374a3-fd1e-563a-bc82-ef9476203959" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a6f99b8f-3a5a-5ef1-bccb-09ce2846b404" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6f99b8f-3a5a-5ef1-bccb-09ce2846b404"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6f99b8f-3a5a-5ef1-bccb-09ce2846b404" :answer/id #uuid "a6f99b8f-3a5a-5ef1-bccb-09ce2846b404" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2244q^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-af367d3a-cdad-5fce-b0de-9044800e4633" :activity/id #uuid "af367d3a-cdad-5fce-b0de-9044800e4633" :activity/title "Modeling with Direct Variation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049281 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-c86fa239-db3c-5048-bcc4-8263276901e2" "step-a99e37c4-23d9-55c1-b8b6-ca1793b52727" "step-f590571b-7252-57ff-b911-5ccaa64a69e4"] :activity/first-step "step-c86fa239-db3c-5048-bcc4-8263276901e2" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-c86fa239-db3c-5048-bcc4-8263276901e2" :step/id #uuid "c86fa239-db3c-5048-bcc4-8263276901e2" :step/content "question-6bd84e69-7c5f-5a4e-bce4-f665a1006214" :step/next "step-a99e37c4-23d9-55c1-b8b6-ca1793b52727" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a99e37c4-23d9-55c1-b8b6-ca1793b52727" :step/id #uuid "a99e37c4-23d9-55c1-b8b6-ca1793b52727" :step/content "question-52c4a416-f053-5e55-99b6-12fd0ef1b322" :step/next "step-f590571b-7252-57ff-b911-5ccaa64a69e4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f590571b-7252-57ff-b911-5ccaa64a69e4" :step/id #uuid "f590571b-7252-57ff-b911-5ccaa64a69e4" :step/content "question-493093e8-547a-52cb-ae1e-43635271726b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124773 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124615 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2001aca6-021f-51d2-9ef2-92bba5a3a5a9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2001aca6-021f-51d2-9ef2-92bba5a3a5a9" :question/id #uuid "2001aca6-021f-51d2-9ef2-92bba5a3a5a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-135313" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.3 & 0 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.45 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.25 & 0.4\\end{bmatrix},\\,q=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{18}{65} \\\\ \\frac{30}{65} \\\\ \\frac{17}{65}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $q$ is a stochastic vector\n\nII. $Pq=q$\n\nIII. $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have \n\n$$\nPq=\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.3 & 0 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.45 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.25 & 0.4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{18}{65} \\\\ \\frac{30}{65} \\\\ \\frac{17}{65}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{65}+\\frac{9}{65}+0 \\\\ \\frac{6.3}{65}+\\frac{13.5}{65}+\\frac{10.2}{65} \\\\ \\frac{2.7}{65}+\\frac{7.5}{65}+\\frac{6.8}{65}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{18}{65} \\\\ \\frac{30}{65} \\\\ \\frac{17}{65}\\end{bmatrix}=q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector such that $Pq=q.$ So, it's a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-55d9c9a4-bfde-5bd4-b59e-36fd1d241250"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-55d9c9a4-bfde-5bd4-b59e-36fd1d241250" :answer-field/id #uuid "55d9c9a4-bfde-5bd4-b59e-36fd1d241250" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1ef6cbc2-9527-5c4a-b3fb-af45a02579cf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-96526529-e366-5b8c-bc8b-f39d7129270f" "answer-1ef6cbc2-9527-5c4a-b3fb-af45a02579cf" "answer-2fcc368e-ff7d-583c-987f-3674a47ece51" "answer-a13ecaef-26d3-57e0-b3ba-3271c0005758" "answer-0a6c4c14-fa02-5f31-bd54-0657abba4c2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96526529-e366-5b8c-bc8b-f39d7129270f" :answer/id #uuid "96526529-e366-5b8c-bc8b-f39d7129270f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ef6cbc2-9527-5c4a-b3fb-af45a02579cf" :answer/id #uuid "1ef6cbc2-9527-5c4a-b3fb-af45a02579cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fcc368e-ff7d-583c-987f-3674a47ece51" :answer/id #uuid "2fcc368e-ff7d-583c-987f-3674a47ece51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a13ecaef-26d3-57e0-b3ba-3271c0005758" :answer/id #uuid "a13ecaef-26d3-57e0-b3ba-3271c0005758" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a6c4c14-fa02-5f31-bd54-0657abba4c2c" :answer/id #uuid "0a6c4c14-fa02-5f31-bd54-0657abba4c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-56fd0998-bb06-5998-a60b-520c9c7f0ced" :activity/id #uuid "56fd0998-bb06-5998-a60b-520c9c7f0ced" :activity/title "Steady-State Vectors" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048393 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-7950fcc1-0b95-59d2-b7e9-f51dd6540cc1" "step-21f93e1c-b14b-5b4b-9122-02e68376a76a" "step-50cc8199-756e-5cf4-addb-4f2e494fb41f" "step-432ba657-a362-5709-a218-2f2609d159ce" "step-c7a9659a-3fe4-58a1-b326-0dbab19d4e9b"] :activity/first-step "step-7950fcc1-0b95-59d2-b7e9-f51dd6540cc1" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7950fcc1-0b95-59d2-b7e9-f51dd6540cc1" :step/id #uuid "7950fcc1-0b95-59d2-b7e9-f51dd6540cc1" :step/content 17592186124773 :step/next "step-21f93e1c-b14b-5b4b-9122-02e68376a76a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-21f93e1c-b14b-5b4b-9122-02e68376a76a" :step/id #uuid "21f93e1c-b14b-5b4b-9122-02e68376a76a" :step/content 17592186124775 :step/next "step-50cc8199-756e-5cf4-addb-4f2e494fb41f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-50cc8199-756e-5cf4-addb-4f2e494fb41f" :step/id #uuid "50cc8199-756e-5cf4-addb-4f2e494fb41f" :step/content "question-2001aca6-021f-51d2-9ef2-92bba5a3a5a9" :step/next "step-432ba657-a362-5709-a218-2f2609d159ce" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-432ba657-a362-5709-a218-2f2609d159ce" :step/id #uuid "432ba657-a362-5709-a218-2f2609d159ce" :step/content 17592186269030 :step/next "step-c7a9659a-3fe4-58a1-b326-0dbab19d4e9b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c7a9659a-3fe4-58a1-b326-0dbab19d4e9b" :step/id #uuid "c7a9659a-3fe4-58a1-b326-0dbab19d4e9b" :step/content 17592186269057 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078436 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f76581a2-daa4-550c-b579-94540f5aa5ee" "question-96ea02ed-6d88-5b00-815c-f8be25c4ea42"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f76581a2-daa4-550c-b579-94540f5aa5ee" :question/id #uuid "f76581a2-daa4-550c-b579-94540f5aa5ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-63977" :question/problem "What is the index of the term $96$ for the geometric sequence below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=6,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This geometric sequence is given as a recurrence relation, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=6,\\,r=4.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in finding $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=96.$ Using the formula for the $n$th term, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\ 96 & =6\\cdot {4}^{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{96}{6} & ={4}^{n-1} \\\\ 16 & ={4}^{n-1} \\\\ {4}^{2} & ={4}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents gives:\n\n$$\n2=n-1\\,⟹\\,n=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $96$ is the $3$rd term of the sequence." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2e19b73d-cabe-517c-9e65-72cddd518722"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2e19b73d-cabe-517c-9e65-72cddd518722" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e19b73d-cabe-517c-9e65-72cddd518722" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-56e179c3-86b2-5a02-b674-d9a1a939689c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56e179c3-86b2-5a02-b674-d9a1a939689c" "answer-96927bba-3ed8-5280-a942-2dfccd2e993b" "answer-2b2662e2-28f0-51b7-9fa7-ba07f2de0f16" "answer-40996b84-32b7-51ec-905b-ddfdf12f19b9" "answer-9d6146d2-2330-51c3-80dd-b7396e3f5dd6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56e179c3-86b2-5a02-b674-d9a1a939689c" :answer/id #uuid "56e179c3-86b2-5a02-b674-d9a1a939689c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96927bba-3ed8-5280-a942-2dfccd2e993b" :answer/id #uuid "96927bba-3ed8-5280-a942-2dfccd2e993b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b2662e2-28f0-51b7-9fa7-ba07f2de0f16" :answer/id #uuid "2b2662e2-28f0-51b7-9fa7-ba07f2de0f16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40996b84-32b7-51ec-905b-ddfdf12f19b9" :answer/id #uuid "40996b84-32b7-51ec-905b-ddfdf12f19b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d6146d2-2330-51c3-80dd-b7396e3f5dd6" :answer/id #uuid "9d6146d2-2330-51c3-80dd-b7396e3f5dd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-96ea02ed-6d88-5b00-815c-f8be25c4ea42" :question/id #uuid "96ea02ed-6d88-5b00-815c-f8be25c4ea42" :question/math-academy-id "q-63978" :question/problem "What is the index of the term $640$ for the geometric sequence below?\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=4f(n),\\,f(1)=10,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This geometric sequence is given as a recurrence relation, i.e.,\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=r\\cdot f(n).\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\nf(1)=10,\\,r=4.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in finding $n$ such that $f(n)=640.$ Using the formula for the $n$th term, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\ 640 & =10\\cdot {4}^{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{640}{10} & ={4}^{n-1} \\\\ 64 & ={4}^{n-1} \\\\ {4}^{3} & ={4}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents gives:\n\n$$\n3=n-1\\,⟹\\,n=4\n$$\n\nTherefore, $640$ is the $4$th term of the sequence." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-00ed5582-4e3e-5fcb-9fc3-a83454376310"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-00ed5582-4e3e-5fcb-9fc3-a83454376310" :answer-field/id #uuid "00ed5582-4e3e-5fcb-9fc3-a83454376310" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1aae7201-0fed-53fc-a560-be8854d1fa86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1aae7201-0fed-53fc-a560-be8854d1fa86" "answer-9306cacc-8d60-5b87-8b47-e67068d937e4" "answer-619a7f6a-6521-5fab-8631-a66510798252" "answer-688648e4-8fd7-5010-8190-cf083062eac1" "answer-c7619aae-7b10-5fbe-b77e-14e4e7134260"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1aae7201-0fed-53fc-a560-be8854d1fa86" :answer/id #uuid "1aae7201-0fed-53fc-a560-be8854d1fa86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9306cacc-8d60-5b87-8b47-e67068d937e4" :answer/id #uuid "9306cacc-8d60-5b87-8b47-e67068d937e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-619a7f6a-6521-5fab-8631-a66510798252" :answer/id #uuid "619a7f6a-6521-5fab-8631-a66510798252" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-688648e4-8fd7-5010-8190-cf083062eac1" :answer/id #uuid "688648e4-8fd7-5010-8190-cf083062eac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7619aae-7b10-5fbe-b77e-14e4e7134260" :answer/id #uuid "c7619aae-7b10-5fbe-b77e-14e4e7134260" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078565 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5f336a0d-d13a-5e94-83e6-97790680d0c6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f336a0d-d13a-5e94-83e6-97790680d0c6" :question/id #uuid "5f336a0d-d13a-5e94-83e6-97790680d0c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-67482" :question/problem "Given that a geometric sequence has the $4$th term ${a}_{4}=250$ and the common ratio $r=5$, what is the index of the term $1\\,250?$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that ${a}_{4}=250$, we can use the formula for the $n$th term to solve for ${a}_{1}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{4-1} \\\\ 250 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{4-1} \\\\ 250 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{250}{125} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} &=2\\cdot {5}^{n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=1\\,250,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\,250 & =2\\cdot {5}^{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{1\\,250}{2} & ={5}^{n-1} \\\\ 625 & ={5}^{n-1} \\\\ {5}^{4} & ={5}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents gives:\n\n$$\n4=n-1\\,⟹\\,n=5\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4c632047-5477-54e3-8a2f-d791ae58065c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4c632047-5477-54e3-8a2f-d791ae58065c" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c632047-5477-54e3-8a2f-d791ae58065c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d2c9e500-94c8-5652-86b9-f435bc1248ef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2bd4e7d8-50eb-5592-9e14-57d4fe27d0e6" "answer-8a8e13ad-2f9f-5475-93