ain diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{43} & =1\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7aa324b6-3e91-5494-bd13-2d7b776cb2de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7aa324b6-3e91-5494-bd13-2d7b776cb2de" :answer-field/id #uuid "7aa324b6-3e91-5494-bd13-2d7b776cb2de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-44fd2f3d-d625-5932-98a6-b9546688bf21" :answer-field/choices ["answer-876ed599-7e89-5bca-ad71-46d6f62d0da4" "answer-24951644-72c8-5d42-8921-b19718af8e7b" "answer-07858392-ccae-557f-aa5f-9ee3e96be02c" "answer-44fd2f3d-d625-5932-98a6-b9546688bf21" "answer-04919aac-89c7-5b2c-b7ec-73705a31ac8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-876ed599-7e89-5bca-ad71-46d6f62d0da4" :answer/id #uuid "876ed599-7e89-5bca-ad71-46d6f62d0da4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24951644-72c8-5d42-8921-b19718af8e7b" :answer/id #uuid "24951644-72c8-5d42-8921-b19718af8e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07858392-ccae-557f-aa5f-9ee3e96be02c" :answer/id #uuid "07858392-ccae-557f-aa5f-9ee3e96be02c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44fd2f3d-d625-5932-98a6-b9546688bf21" :answer/id #uuid "44fd2f3d-d625-5932-98a6-b9546688bf21" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04919aac-89c7-5b2c-b7ec-73705a31ac8e" :answer/id #uuid "04919aac-89c7-5b2c-b7ec-73705a31ac8e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-40b938cb-f23c-5d0f-a251-58ee4d72d0a4" :question/id #uuid "40b938cb-f23c-5d0f-a251-58ee4d72d0a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126346" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{21} & =2\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =-2\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-21fd3325-4b20-503e-aa47-2866327e5755"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-21fd3325-4b20-503e-aa47-2866327e5755" :answer-field/id #uuid "21fd3325-4b20-503e-aa47-2866327e5755" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f5e8ff6c-fa2e-535e-8eb3-bac7d856c93c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5e8ff6c-fa2e-535e-8eb3-bac7d856c93c" "answer-a6d2da48-1096-562d-9e36-90de522e519d" "answer-46ddff2f-c494-5d61-ad24-7e5bbd050df6" "answer-fbb2c99c-855e-51cd-9c61-17446ce611d2" "answer-75d1fd80-24ee-57d2-a928-062949585d3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5e8ff6c-fa2e-535e-8eb3-bac7d856c93c" :answer/id #uuid "f5e8ff6c-fa2e-535e-8eb3-bac7d856c93c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6d2da48-1096-562d-9e36-90de522e519d" :answer/id #uuid "a6d2da48-1096-562d-9e36-90de522e519d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46ddff2f-c494-5d61-ad24-7e5bbd050df6" :answer/id #uuid "46ddff2f-c494-5d61-ad24-7e5bbd050df6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbb2c99c-855e-51cd-9c61-17446ce611d2" :answer/id #uuid "fbb2c99c-855e-51cd-9c61-17446ce611d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75d1fd80-24ee-57d2-a928-062949585d3a" :answer/id #uuid "75d1fd80-24ee-57d2-a928-062949585d3a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119784 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5fc95051-8b70-5447-aece-290d3854c40e" "question-814b1f0e-0432-56a4-8a3b-10efb7462756" "question-e901e3e2-6ad0-5a4e-b4c9-fb5111610c41"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5fc95051-8b70-5447-aece-290d3854c40e" :question/id #uuid "5fc95051-8b70-5447-aece-290d3854c40e" :question/math-academy-id "q-126481" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $D$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $D$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${D}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $D$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $D$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${D}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{D}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8fe26995-771e-5e1a-8bdf-3ca759f26bd9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8fe26995-771e-5e1a-8bdf-3ca759f26bd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fe26995-771e-5e1a-8bdf-3ca759f26bd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dc8c2bed-cb94-57d8-9276-32a0fd10323b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-14c7d084-e531-5ec8-b8a4-84313c9c5235" "answer-309105f2-241b-59a8-b108-1fbc5ad23672" "answer-dc8c2bed-cb94-57d8-9276-32a0fd10323b" "answer-1772de48-db0b-51da-aed0-d21f58c33bb2" "answer-5046e838-51c7-590f-9148-f9c9e26829ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14c7d084-e531-5ec8-b8a4-84313c9c5235" :answer/id #uuid "14c7d084-e531-5ec8-b8a4-84313c9c5235" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-309105f2-241b-59a8-b108-1fbc5ad23672" :answer/id #uuid "309105f2-241b-59a8-b108-1fbc5ad23672" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc8c2bed-cb94-57d8-9276-32a0fd10323b" :answer/id #uuid "dc8c2bed-cb94-57d8-9276-32a0fd10323b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1772de48-db0b-51da-aed0-d21f58c33bb2" :answer/id #uuid "1772de48-db0b-51da-aed0-d21f58c33bb2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5046e838-51c7-590f-9148-f9c9e26829ff" :answer/id #uuid "5046e838-51c7-590f-9148-f9c9e26829ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-814b1f0e-0432-56a4-8a3b-10efb7462756" :question/id #uuid "814b1f0e-0432-56a4-8a3b-10efb7462756" :question/math-academy-id "q-126474" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $B$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $B$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${B}^{T}+B$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true, since the result of ${B}^{T}+B$ has all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{B}^{T}+B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9b102253-6f2b-5abd-a982-625362c5bac1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b102253-6f2b-5abd-a982-625362c5bac1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b102253-6f2b-5abd-a982-625362c5bac1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-de7db33e-db49-51d2-a800-9aafb37e46d3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-959c3d53-f156-5e94-9bfd-bec522413d33" "answer-6ba37546-0b19-5c70-a714-0a34b98342c1" "answer-82a96621-2960-553c-91f5-72e8e13d6f3c" "answer-4c4d8db6-cf00-5561-9f71-cda33196d5a4" "answer-de7db33e-db49-51d2-a800-9aafb37e46d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-959c3d53-f156-5e94-9bfd-bec522413d33" :answer/id #uuid "959c3d53-f156-5e94-9bfd-bec522413d33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ba37546-0b19-5c70-a714-0a34b98342c1" :answer/id #uuid "6ba37546-0b19-5c70-a714-0a34b98342c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82a96621-2960-553c-91f5-72e8e13d6f3c" :answer/id #uuid "82a96621-2960-553c-91f5-72e8e13d6f3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c4d8db6-cf00-5561-9f71-cda33196d5a4" :answer/id #uuid "4c4d8db6-cf00-5561-9f71-cda33196d5a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de7db33e-db49-51d2-a800-9aafb37e46d3" :answer/id #uuid "de7db33e-db49-51d2-a800-9aafb37e46d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e901e3e2-6ad0-5a4e-b4c9-fb5111610c41" :question/id #uuid "e901e3e2-6ad0-5a4e-b4c9-fb5111610c41" :question/math-academy-id "q-42114" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $A$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${A}^{T}$ is lower triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since ${A}^{T}$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4ee22029-c16e-5aeb-adc2-4fcc4a68c015"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4ee22029-c16e-5aeb-adc2-4fcc4a68c015" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee22029-c16e-5aeb-adc2-4fcc4a68c015" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-54aa0d5a-e3d8-51a9-8f3b-dff607ae904f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5d551e2f-4165-511c-9380-cb5230ba4f24" "answer-732dcb76-f25b-5bba-ba60-def211538974" "answer-bd949b47-98d3-5daf-9d62-c468035cb5ec" "answer-e5620cdc-dc79-59a5-961b-bec9724caa10" "answer-54aa0d5a-e3d8-51a9-8f3b-dff607ae904f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d551e2f-4165-511c-9380-cb5230ba4f24" :answer/id #uuid "5d551e2f-4165-511c-9380-cb5230ba4f24" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-732dcb76-f25b-5bba-ba60-def211538974" :answer/id #uuid "732dcb76-f25b-5bba-ba60-def211538974" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd949b47-98d3-5daf-9d62-c468035cb5ec" :answer/id #uuid "bd949b47-98d3-5daf-9d62-c468035cb5ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5620cdc-dc79-59a5-961b-bec9724caa10" :answer/id #uuid "e5620cdc-dc79-59a5-961b-bec9724caa10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54aa0d5a-e3d8-51a9-8f3b-dff607ae904f" :answer/id #uuid "54aa0d5a-e3d8-51a9-8f3b-dff607ae904f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119999 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096617 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d8004d91-2319-5283-80d1-a0670d83fdc0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d8004d91-2319-5283-80d1-a0670d83fdc0" :question/id #uuid "d8004d91-2319-5283-80d1-a0670d83fdc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-104300" :question/problem "Differentiate ${x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={x}^{3}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({x}^{3})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+({x}^{3})(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4d091bc-16c4-5784-a6c4-28309a12be4c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4d091bc-16c4-5784-a6c4-28309a12be4c" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4d091bc-16c4-5784-a6c4-28309a12be4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a462a7c9-b56d-5b3e-b5f2-01b27202da04" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd2fd5e5-1d32-56a9-b43f-1421f5392621" "answer-cadbcaa0-5f4b-5598-a6eb-4541c20a3865" "answer-4fbb081d-8fbf-5577-b042-226064e10be0" "answer-a462a7c9-b56d-5b3e-b5f2-01b27202da04" "answer-a20a9a53-3e6f-5754-8799-d24e521ac2b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd2fd5e5-1d32-56a9-b43f-1421f5392621" :answer/id #uuid "dd2fd5e5-1d32-56a9-b43f-1421f5392621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cadbcaa0-5f4b-5598-a6eb-4541c20a3865" :answer/id #uuid "cadbcaa0-5f4b-5598-a6eb-4541c20a3865" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fbb081d-8fbf-5577-b042-226064e10be0" :answer/id #uuid "4fbb081d-8fbf-5577-b042-226064e10be0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a462a7c9-b56d-5b3e-b5f2-01b27202da04" :answer/id #uuid "a462a7c9-b56d-5b3e-b5f2-01b27202da04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a20a9a53-3e6f-5754-8799-d24e521ac2b0" :answer/id #uuid "a20a9a53-3e6f-5754-8799-d24e521ac2b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096618 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-303e2b76-22b6-55f6-abfa-1986d9ab5f9d" "question-f475b19b-1e35-517e-8f15-4fa3d740b6ba"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-303e2b76-22b6-55f6-abfa-1986d9ab5f9d" :question/id #uuid "303e2b76-22b6-55f6-abfa-1986d9ab5f9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-320820" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\operatorname{log}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n**Hint:** $\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)={log}_{10}⁡(x)$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x))}^{′}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x){(\\operatorname{log}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({sec}^{2}⁡(x))(\\operatorname{log}⁡(x))+(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x))(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0af8eb9f-fc24-5d73-ad75-f548e3ea3646"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0af8eb9f-fc24-5d73-ad75-f548e3ea3646" :answer-field/id #uuid "0af8eb9f-fc24-5d73-ad75-f548e3ea3646" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f7864c3b-b764-56cd-a641-bd65ea7dd484" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7864c3b-b764-56cd-a641-bd65ea7dd484"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7864c3b-b764-56cd-a641-bd65ea7dd484" :answer/id #uuid "f7864c3b-b764-56cd-a641-bd65ea7dd484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sec^{2}(x)\\log(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f475b19b-1e35-517e-8f15-4fa3d740b6ba" :question/id #uuid "f475b19b-1e35-517e-8f15-4fa3d740b6ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-320824" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}+3$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2}+3)}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+({x}^{2}+3){(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =(2x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))+({x}^{2}+3)(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+\\frac{{x}^{2}+3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6a34341-fe46-5049-b63f-03fb79ef67af"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6a34341-fe46-5049-b63f-03fb79ef67af" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a34341-fe46-5049-b63f-03fb79ef67af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ddbe9744-04e5-5a13-898b-3293efe4160f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ddbe9744-04e5-5a13-898b-3293efe4160f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddbe9744-04e5-5a13-898b-3293efe4160f" :answer/id #uuid "ddbe9744-04e5-5a13-898b-3293efe4160f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}+3}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096619 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a0fee3ca-7f95-5f0e-a414-4282e409bf7a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a0fee3ca-7f95-5f0e-a414-4282e409bf7a" :question/id #uuid "a0fee3ca-7f95-5f0e-a414-4282e409bf7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-319824" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=1$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=2x+1$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(2x+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+1}{x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=1$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{2x+1}{x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1)+1}{1}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-99aa048f-795f-5835-b3e4-7ab1bb44a8a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-99aa048f-795f-5835-b3e4-7ab1bb44a8a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "99aa048f-795f-5835-b3e4-7ab1bb44a8a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fa1cb47c-2e18-5935-a199-4342ba479343" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa1cb47c-2e18-5935-a199-4342ba479343"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa1cb47c-2e18-5935-a199-4342ba479343" :answer/id #uuid "fa1cb47c-2e18-5935-a199-4342ba479343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097818 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we have the two functions $u(x)=2x^3$ and $v(x)=x^2.$ How do we calculate the derivative of their product $(u(x) \\cdot v(x))'?$\n\nTo do that, we can use the **product rule**, which states that the derivative of the product of two functions is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\left(u(x) \\cdot  v(x)\\right)' = u'(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v'(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the derivatives of the two functions are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(x) & =(2{x}^{3})^{′}=6{x}^{2}, \\\\ {v}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2})^{′}=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we plug all of this into the product rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(x)\\cdot v(x))}^{′} & =(6{x}^{2})({x}^{2})+(2{x}^{3})(2x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{4}+4{x}^{4} \\\\  & =10{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis example was quite simple, and we could have solved it by calculating the product first and then taking the derivative. We can do it now to double check our result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(x)\\cdot v(x))}^{′} & =(2{x}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2})^{′} \\\\  & =(2{x}^{5})^{′} \\\\  & =10{x}^{4}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSometimes, however, we cannot calculate the product algebraically, or it can be tedious to do it. In those cases, the product rule will turn out to be very useful!" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096889 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176342 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176344 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6e4c5edf-99ca-525c-a6e8-fa582f571ea0" :activity/id #uuid "6e4c5edf-99ca-525c-a6e8-fa582f571ea0" :activity/title "Residuals and Residual Plots" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050269 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-fc3683d1-ce01-56ab-b8d9-ad456743c55e" "step-749adcf2-3609-57ef-a88a-58f98584fb0f" "step-2c0eb85e-9eec-5f4f-b6fc-97a5c56860cb"] :activity/first-step "step-fc3683d1-ce01-56ab-b8d9-ad456743c55e" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-fc3683d1-ce01-56ab-b8d9-ad456743c55e" :step/id #uuid "fc3683d1-ce01-56ab-b8d9-ad456743c55e" :step/content 17592186176342 :step/next "step-749adcf2-3609-57ef-a88a-58f98584fb0f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-749adcf2-3609-57ef-a88a-58f98584fb0f" :step/id #uuid "749adcf2-3609-57ef-a88a-58f98584fb0f" :step/content 17592186176344 :step/next "step-2c0eb85e-9eec-5f4f-b6fc-97a5c56860cb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c0eb85e-9eec-5f4f-b6fc-97a5c56860cb" :step/id #uuid "2c0eb85e-9eec-5f4f-b6fc-97a5c56860cb" :step/content 17592186554645 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074207 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074219 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073784 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-215445ba-4b6e-5c24-97c0-9095e5d1fe80"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-215445ba-4b6e-5c24-97c0-9095e5d1fe80" :question/id #uuid "215445ba-4b6e-5c24-97c0-9095e5d1fe80" :question/math-academy-id "q-89719" :question/problem "A triangle $△ABC$ is reflected over the $x$-axis and then translated by $5$ units to the left. If the resulting triangle is $△PQR,$ which of the following statements must be true?\n\nI. $△ABC∼△PQR$\n\nII. $∠A≅∠P$\n\nIII. $5AC=PR$" :question/worked-solution "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations.\n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We are given a combination of a reflection and a translation. As a result, we obtain that \n\n$$\n△ABC∼△PQR.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $△ABC∼△PQR,$ all corresponding angles of the triangles must be congruent. In particular, \n\n$$\n∠A≅∠P.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since our combined transformation consists of rigid motions only (namely, reflection and translation), the distance between all points is preserved under the transformation. Therefore, we obtain that \n\n$$\nAC=PR.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-38ac1c06-8797-54c9-919a-9badd40bf6f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-38ac1c06-8797-54c9-919a-9badd40bf6f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "38ac1c06-8797-54c9-919a-9badd40bf6f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-23e50c1d-2565-52fb-a27d-e5eebdb995f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-23e50c1d-2565-52fb-a27d-e5eebdb995f8" "answer-bfce57ab-0e1b-5406-9ad1-93d01c1c45c0" "answer-37aa1780-0a4d-52e2-9cea-73b9f1b8285f" "answer-28f6047f-9a87-547f-a2b0-63d84f9e7ba0" "answer-a74b9557-7451-5e28-88f9-084444ad33bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23e50c1d-2565-52fb-a27d-e5eebdb995f8" :answer/id #uuid "23e50c1d-2565-52fb-a27d-e5eebdb995f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfce57ab-0e1b-5406-9ad1-93d01c1c45c0" :answer/id #uuid "bfce57ab-0e1b-5406-9ad1-93d01c1c45c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37aa1780-0a4d-52e2-9cea-73b9f1b8285f" :answer/id #uuid "37aa1780-0a4d-52e2-9cea-73b9f1b8285f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28f6047f-9a87-547f-a2b0-63d84f9e7ba0" :answer/id #uuid "28f6047f-9a87-547f-a2b0-63d84f9e7ba0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a74b9557-7451-5e28-88f9-084444ad33bb" :answer/id #uuid "a74b9557-7451-5e28-88f9-084444ad33bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073917 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-19280716-a1d4-5a8a-bdaf-7c2fa87a8518"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-19280716-a1d4-5a8a-bdaf-7c2fa87a8518" :question/id #uuid "19280716-a1d4-5a8a-bdaf-7c2fa87a8518" :question/math-academy-id "q-89723" :question/problem "Which of the following transformations map any polygon to a similar polygon?\n\nI. $(x,y)↦(x-3,y+1)$\n\nII. $(x,y)↦(2x,2y)$\n\nIII. $(x,y)↦(y,-x)$" :question/worked-solution "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations. \n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the transformations in turn.\n\n- Transformation I represents a translation by $3$ units to the left and $1$ unit upward. Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation II represents a dilation of scale factor $2$ and center $O.$ Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation III represents a rotation by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise around the point $O.$ Thus, it is a rigid motion and, therefore, a similarity transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-03cf1212-20cf-5fec-91ff-894cfb864801"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-03cf1212-20cf-5fec-91ff-894cfb864801" :answer-field/id #uuid "03cf1212-20cf-5fec-91ff-894cfb864801" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4d71a682-eaee-5663-bfae-47c7ddc5f646" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7060a78b-a388-5597-a5b4-fc581daeb80f" "answer-407d0955-8691-55fa-b272-acb163e39973" "answer-05427ec8-e02f-5962-a97b-e42a7ce91391" "answer-4d71a682-eaee-5663-bfae-47c7ddc5f646" "answer-13de73f0-fe5e-594f-80cc-4fcff2c06615"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7060a78b-a388-5597-a5b4-fc581daeb80f" :answer/id #uuid "7060a78b-a388-5597-a5b4-fc581daeb80f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-407d0955-8691-55fa-b272-acb163e39973" :answer/id #uuid "407d0955-8691-55fa-b272-acb163e39973" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05427ec8-e02f-5962-a97b-e42a7ce91391" :answer/id #uuid "05427ec8-e02f-5962-a97b-e42a7ce91391" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d71a682-eaee-5663-bfae-47c7ddc5f646" :answer/id #uuid "4d71a682-eaee-5663-bfae-47c7ddc5f646" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13de73f0-fe5e-594f-80cc-4fcff2c06615" :answer/id #uuid "13de73f0-fe5e-594f-80cc-4fcff2c06615" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d9e9c217-5ae3-5068-98fd-e6cb3f9c865d" :activity/id #uuid "d9e9c217-5ae3-5068-98fd-e6cb3f9c865d" :activity/title "Similarity Transformations" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048583 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-cf78c2a0-767a-5134-ad68-8cf1fdecbd91" "step-eca63cc3-1f0e-59ee-b361-58cfcc164925" "step-f3ed4448-d98b-563f-8e2d-4623559201da" "step-1ecfdd56-b7a0-5383-b779-374f5912150a"] :activity/first-step "step-cf78c2a0-767a-5134-ad68-8cf1fdecbd91" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-cf78c2a0-767a-5134-ad68-8cf1fdecbd91" :step/id #uuid "cf78c2a0-767a-5134-ad68-8cf1fdecbd91" :step/content 17592186074207 :step/next "step-eca63cc3-1f0e-59ee-b361-58cfcc164925" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eca63cc3-1f0e-59ee-b361-58cfcc164925" :step/id #uuid "eca63cc3-1f0e-59ee-b361-58cfcc164925" :step/content 17592186074219 :step/next "step-f3ed4448-d98b-563f-8e2d-4623559201da" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f3ed4448-d98b-563f-8e2d-4623559201da" :step/id #uuid "f3ed4448-d98b-563f-8e2d-4623559201da" :step/content "question-215445ba-4b6e-5c24-97c0-9095e5d1fe80" :step/next "step-1ecfdd56-b7a0-5383-b779-374f5912150a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1ecfdd56-b7a0-5383-b779-374f5912150a" :step/id #uuid "1ecfdd56-b7a0-5383-b779-374f5912150a" :step/content "question-19280716-a1d4-5a8a-bdaf-7c2fa87a8518" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064323 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-60cacfbe-5c7a-52cc-86ec-dc2c6a600d4a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-60cacfbe-5c7a-52cc-86ec-dc2c6a600d4a" :question/id #uuid "60cacfbe-5c7a-52cc-86ec-dc2c6a600d4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-2740" :question/problem "Factor $2{t}^{2}+5t{v}^{3}+6{v}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $\\text{GCF}$ of the three terms:\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(2{t}^{2},5t{v}^{3},6{v}^{2})=1\n$$\n\nSince the $\\text{GCF}$ of the three terms is $1$, the given expression cannot be factored any further." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b40158f-c199-5426-b54f-3956c841723d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b40158f-c199-5426-b54f-3956c841723d" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b40158f-c199-5426-b54f-3956c841723d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ce4484aa-f3f4-5bd9-88f1-5c0385dee98b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce4484aa-f3f4-5bd9-88f1-5c0385dee98b" "answer-befda994-40ed-5fd5-82a5-ebfabcf3c853" "answer-c734fab6-5d21-5144-b416-fc359fbaef35" "answer-7725c40c-c7d1-5a07-b1ed-5bc83db25764" "answer-7f0deb1c-6e6d-5201-be46-8acd1f3de62e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce4484aa-f3f4-5bd9-88f1-5c0385dee98b" :answer/id #uuid "ce4484aa-f3f4-5bd9-88f1-5c0385dee98b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{t}^{2}+5t{v}^{3}+6{v}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-befda994-40ed-5fd5-82a5-ebfabcf3c853" :answer/id #uuid "befda994-40ed-5fd5-82a5-ebfabcf3c853" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t(2t+11{v}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c734fab6-5d21-5144-b416-fc359fbaef35" :answer/id #uuid "c734fab6-5d21-5144-b416-fc359fbaef35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t(2t+5{v}^{2}+6{v}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7725c40c-c7d1-5a07-b1ed-5bc83db25764" :answer/id #uuid "7725c40c-c7d1-5a07-b1ed-5bc83db25764" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(2{t}^{2}+5t{v}^{2}+6v)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f0deb1c-6e6d-5201-be46-8acd1f3de62e" :answer/id #uuid "7f0deb1c-6e6d-5201-be46-8acd1f3de62e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{v}^{2}(2{t}^{2}+5t+6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064324 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e2bc30f9-89bd-586d-8e06-36b5ff066cb1" "question-6b40873b-cd99-5437-a84e-b998bb4576d6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e2bc30f9-89bd-586d-8e06-36b5ff066cb1" :question/id #uuid "e2bc30f9-89bd-586d-8e06-36b5ff066cb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-52250" :question/problem "Factor the polynomial expression $x(w-6)-10(w-6).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $\\text{GCF}$ of the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(x(w-6),10(w-6))=w-6\n$$\n\nEach term is already written as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (w-6)-10\\cdot (w-6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (w-6)-10\\cdot (w-6) & = \\\\ (x-10)(w-6) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2708da49-07a5-536d-a886-c5f8ed22fc70"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2708da49-07a5-536d-a886-c5f8ed22fc70" :answer-field/id #uuid "2708da49-07a5-536d-a886-c5f8ed22fc70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ae6a0a05-29ac-5657-8660-18b7cdfba4cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae6a0a05-29ac-5657-8660-18b7cdfba4cb" "answer-2abccb54-16a1-565a-a3d7-7b17784660fe" "answer-66ae83bc-77cf-51f1-a087-6bdd8ac365c1" "answer-7895f872-6b80-5972-8cff-a79b32fa8e44" "answer-a36b2445-43ae-55ce-a7aa-df740ce6b8f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae6a0a05-29ac-5657-8660-18b7cdfba4cb" :answer/id #uuid "ae6a0a05-29ac-5657-8660-18b7cdfba4cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-10)(w-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2abccb54-16a1-565a-a3d7-7b17784660fe" :answer/id #uuid "2abccb54-16a1-565a-a3d7-7b17784660fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-6)(w-10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66ae83bc-77cf-51f1-a087-6bdd8ac365c1" :answer/id #uuid "66ae83bc-77cf-51f1-a087-6bdd8ac365c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10(w-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7895f872-6b80-5972-8cff-a79b32fa8e44" :answer/id #uuid "7895f872-6b80-5972-8cff-a79b32fa8e44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10x(w-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a36b2445-43ae-55ce-a7aa-df740ce6b8f0" :answer/id #uuid "a36b2445-43ae-55ce-a7aa-df740ce6b8f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(w-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6b40873b-cd99-5437-a84e-b998bb4576d6" :question/id #uuid "6b40873b-cd99-5437-a84e-b998bb4576d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-52275" :question/problem "Factor the polynomial expression $p({s}^{2}-11)-12({s}^{2}-11).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $\\text{GCF}$ of the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(p({s}^{2}-11),12({s}^{2}-11))={s}^{2}-11\n$$\n\nEach term is already written as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot ({s}^{2}-11)-12\\cdot ({s}^{2}-11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot ({s}^{2}-11)-12\\cdot ({s}^{2}-11) & = \\\\ (p-12)({s}^{2}-11) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-069a8ba6-90f3-5bde-b0e0-93af47e1ca96"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-069a8ba6-90f3-5bde-b0e0-93af47e1ca96" :answer-field/id #uuid "069a8ba6-90f3-5bde-b0e0-93af47e1ca96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-32002788-a360-5052-ae64-5689e34590f4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8a948e4-12fe-5885-adb8-61fce698c6ed" "answer-d58b1732-c1c0-510d-8b42-66c08129e6a1" "answer-32002788-a360-5052-ae64-5689e34590f4" "answer-b4209178-f9e4-5a9e-b002-8f82ea618938" "answer-11048dc5-c619-5b38-9741-5859a2f2a50f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8a948e4-12fe-5885-adb8-61fce698c6ed" :answer/id #uuid "b8a948e4-12fe-5885-adb8-61fce698c6ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(12-p)({s}^{2}-11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d58b1732-c1c0-510d-8b42-66c08129e6a1" :answer/id #uuid "d58b1732-c1c0-510d-8b42-66c08129e6a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(p-11)({s}^{2}-12)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32002788-a360-5052-ae64-5689e34590f4" :answer/id #uuid "32002788-a360-5052-ae64-5689e34590f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(p-12)({s}^{2}-11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4209178-f9e4-5a9e-b002-8f82ea618938" :answer/id #uuid "b4209178-f9e4-5a9e-b002-8f82ea618938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11(p-12)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11048dc5-c619-5b38-9741-5859a2f2a50f" :answer/id #uuid "11048dc5-c619-5b38-9741-5859a2f2a50f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p(s-11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b2618742-1884-586e-9829-b1e11578dd38" :activity/id #uuid "b2618742-1884-586e-9829-b1e11578dd38" :activity/title "Factoring Polynomials Using GCFs" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051017 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-7f0926e4-9b33-5df4-b283-a705cc5ebc64" "step-69058107-d847-5a32-9c70-82ea679d1eba" "step-f2551290-cf86-5ec0-b279-c039286a9eb0"] :activity/first-step "step-7f0926e4-9b33-5df4-b283-a705cc5ebc64" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7f0926e4-9b33-5df4-b283-a705cc5ebc64" :step/id #uuid "7f0926e4-9b33-5df4-b283-a705cc5ebc64" :step/content "question-60cacfbe-5c7a-52cc-86ec-dc2c6a600d4a" :step/next "step-69058107-d847-5a32-9c70-82ea679d1eba" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-69058107-d847-5a32-9c70-82ea679d1eba" :step/id #uuid "69058107-d847-5a32-9c70-82ea679d1eba" :step/content "question-e2bc30f9-89bd-586d-8e06-36b5ff066cb1" :step/next "step-f2551290-cf86-5ec0-b279-c039286a9eb0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f2551290-cf86-5ec0-b279-c039286a9eb0" :step/id #uuid "f2551290-cf86-5ec0-b279-c039286a9eb0" :step/content "question-6b40873b-cd99-5437-a84e-b998bb4576d6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a462519c-8f3a-5164-b4fe-0415a57a0df2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a462519c-8f3a-5164-b4fe-0415a57a0df2" :question/id #uuid "a462519c-8f3a-5164-b4fe-0415a57a0df2" :question/math-academy-id "q-106707" :question/problem "Let $B$ be the set of all functions $f:Q\\to Q$ such that $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. For each $f(x)\\in B$, we have $-f(x)\\in B$ such that $f(x)+(-f(x))=0.$\n\nII. For any $f(x),g(x),h(x)\\in B,$ we have $[f(x)-g(x)]+h(x)=f(x)-[g(x)+h(x)].$\n\nIII. The addition of functions in $B$ is commutative." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider a function $f(x)\\in B$ where $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Then $-f(x)$ is the corresponding negative function such that\n\n$$\nf(x)+(-f(x))=f(x)-f(x)=0.\n$$\n\nHowever,\n\n$$\n-f(0)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\ne \\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nand, hence, $-f(x)\\notin B.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2},$ $g(x)=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $h(x)=2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2},$ from $B.$ Then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[f(x)-g(x)]+h(x) & =[{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}]+2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ f(x)-[g(x)+h(x)] & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-[\\frac{1}{2}+2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-[2{x}^{2}+1] \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-2{x}^{2}-1 \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $[f(x)-g(x)]+h(x)\\ne f(x)-[g(x)+h(x)].$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(x),g(x)\\in B,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\nf(x)+g(x)=g(x)+f(x)\n$$\n\nsince the addition of functions is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c1667ad-3207-5d60-a6a8-63d80d6cb9a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c1667ad-3207-5d60-a6a8-63d80d6cb9a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1667ad-3207-5d60-a6a8-63d80d6cb9a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-69dde657-e455-50ff-8100-f03b5ebb558e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e28a5398-d9ed-502e-977d-28d4a3a660ea" "answer-db423193-4755-5aa1-a9f5-871e3febcb41" "answer-84ec3e14-db65-5d8c-a804-512729ac558b" "answer-2f39c98f-ab2e-5734-97cd-7535d4b97fcf" "answer-69dde657-e455-50ff-8100-f03b5ebb558e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e28a5398-d9ed-502e-977d-28d4a3a660ea" :answer/id #uuid "e28a5398-d9ed-502e-977d-28d4a3a660ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db423193-4755-5aa1-a9f5-871e3febcb41" :answer/id #uuid "db423193-4755-5aa1-a9f5-871e3febcb41" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84ec3e14-db65-5d8c-a804-512729ac558b" :answer/id #uuid "84ec3e14-db65-5d8c-a804-512729ac558b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f39c98f-ab2e-5734-97cd-7535d4b97fcf" :answer/id #uuid "2f39c98f-ab2e-5734-97cd-7535d4b97fcf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69dde657-e455-50ff-8100-f03b5ebb558e" :answer/id #uuid "69dde657-e455-50ff-8100-f03b5ebb558e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-34bd5220-616c-5a5a-8d4a-800215bc060f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-34bd5220-616c-5a5a-8d4a-800215bc060f" :question/id #uuid "34bd5220-616c-5a5a-8d4a-800215bc060f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106808" :question/problem "Let $V$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant $0.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. The zero-matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $V.$\n\nII. Scalar multiplication of matrices in $V$ is associative.\n\nIII. For any $A,B\\in V$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (A+B)=\\alpha A+\\alpha B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}=0.$ Hence, $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in V.$\n\n- Statements II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in V,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta {a}_{ij})=(\\alpha \\beta ){a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta A)=(\\alpha \\beta )A.\n$$\n\n- Statements III is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ and $B=({b}_{ij})$ from $V,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha ({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij})=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\alpha {b}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24e8cec7-9fe1-550d-b2c4-3278855ff161"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24e8cec7-9fe1-550d-b2c4-3278855ff161" :answer-field/id #uuid "24e8cec7-9fe1-550d-b2c4-3278855ff161" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-42f06bdc-fc44-5416-b54e-e9da22de7c99" :answer-field/choices ["answer-30417482-b0cb-5c67-9257-691a127096fc" "answer-71191412-90b2-5f96-8f3a-8411a9f63974" "answer-910f4cad-1f61-5bcb-a59a-b80fceb4f6f1" "answer-42f06bdc-fc44-5416-b54e-e9da22de7c99" "answer-d813b1cc-a05e-50d0-816b-fe43a3ca3e8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30417482-b0cb-5c67-9257-691a127096fc" :answer/id #uuid "30417482-b0cb-5c67-9257-691a127096fc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71191412-90b2-5f96-8f3a-8411a9f63974" :answer/id #uuid "71191412-90b2-5f96-8f3a-8411a9f63974" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-910f4cad-1f61-5bcb-a59a-b80fceb4f6f1" :answer/id #uuid "910f4cad-1f61-5bcb-a59a-b80fceb4f6f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42f06bdc-fc44-5416-b54e-e9da22de7c99" :answer/id #uuid "42f06bdc-fc44-5416-b54e-e9da22de7c99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d813b1cc-a05e-50d0-816b-fe43a3ca3e8e" :answer/id #uuid "d813b1cc-a05e-50d0-816b-fe43a3ca3e8e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059696 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3bef771f-b5d0-5c41-9326-f619dd4a81a0" "question-f6cb1c6c-0f55-5843-930a-ea6ae4ca9cd3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3bef771f-b5d0-5c41-9326-f619dd4a81a0" :question/id #uuid "3bef771f-b5d0-5c41-9326-f619dd4a81a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-182448" :question/problem "$\\,$ $1$ is not prime and $1$ is not composite.\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?" :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's law posits that the negation of a conjunction of two statements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,¬(1\\text{ is not prime}\\text{ and }1\\text{ is not composite}) & ≡¬((1\\text{ is not prime})∧(1\\text{ is not composite})) \\\\  & ≡¬(1\\text{ is not prime})∨¬(1\\text{ is not composite}) \\\\  & ≡(1\\text{ is prime})∨(1\\text{ is composite}) \\\\  & ≡1\\text{ is prime}\\text{ or }1\\text{ is composite}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9bb2af0-5705-5445-9172-3e31bec4a94b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9bb2af0-5705-5445-9172-3e31bec4a94b" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9bb2af0-5705-5445-9172-3e31bec4a94b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-80e50271-3f25-55c7-9cd0-f2b350996515" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9253cc5b-e263-5306-9ff3-c2980f041b0c" "answer-8e737564-ed49-57bf-975a-18d404aba85e" "answer-a72792d4-a7b0-549b-b478-335fe4d3b716" "answer-80e50271-3f25-55c7-9cd0-f2b350996515" "answer-8ed4ff08-bf9c-5c19-830a-c288e415b38b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9253cc5b-e263-5306-9ff3-c2980f041b0c" :answer/id #uuid "9253cc5b-e263-5306-9ff3-c2980f041b0c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ is not prime or $1$ is not composite" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e737564-ed49-57bf-975a-18d404aba85e" :answer/id #uuid "8e737564-ed49-57bf-975a-18d404aba85e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ is prime and $1$ is composite" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a72792d4-a7b0-549b-b478-335fe4d3b716" :answer/id #uuid "a72792d4-a7b0-549b-b478-335fe4d3b716" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ is prime and $1$ is not composite" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80e50271-3f25-55c7-9cd0-f2b350996515" :answer/id #uuid "80e50271-3f25-55c7-9cd0-f2b350996515" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ is prime or $1$ is composite" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ed4ff08-bf9c-5c19-830a-c288e415b38b" :answer/id #uuid "8ed4ff08-bf9c-5c19-830a-c288e415b38b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ is prime or $1$ is not composite" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f6cb1c6c-0f55-5843-930a-ea6ae4ca9cd3" :question/id #uuid "f6cb1c6c-0f55-5843-930a-ea6ae4ca9cd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-182441" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x$ is prime and $x$ is odd.\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?" :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's law posits that the negation of a conjunction of two statements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(x\\text{ is prime}\\text{ and }x\\text{ is odd}) & ≡¬((x\\text{ is prime})∧(x\\text{ is odd})) \\\\  & ≡¬(x\\text{ is prime})∨¬(x\\text{ is odd}) \\\\  & ≡(x\\text{ is not prime})∨(x\\text{ is even}) \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not prime}\\text{ or }x\\text{ is even}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b8601b2-92aa-5f8b-87af-4b7a55ebbae4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b8601b2-92aa-5f8b-87af-4b7a55ebbae4" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b8601b2-92aa-5f8b-87af-4b7a55ebbae4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ffa1df0d-e6d7-5117-92d7-78580b573150" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c5f3662-43e5-5841-a5cf-42b69470daef" "answer-2553d01b-7172-559c-afbd-8e32700691dc" "answer-ffa1df0d-e6d7-5117-92d7-78580b573150" "answer-c7470ec4-1efa-5556-b1b6-87b10810db7f" "answer-d38d9b90-26a9-5522-8888-b37bd17e24ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c5f3662-43e5-5841-a5cf-42b69470daef" :answer/id #uuid "7c5f3662-43e5-5841-a5cf-