b97be0c78" :question/math-academy-id "q-1485" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬((Q∧P)∨R)$ using De Morgan's laws." :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(Q∧P)≡¬P∨¬R, \\\\ ¬(Q∨P)≡¬P∧¬Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬((Q∧P)∨R) & ≡¬(Q∧P)∧¬R \\\\  & ≡(¬Q∨¬P)∧¬R\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e6095939-f405-593b-8b71-6f9b5f58ed79"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6095939-f405-593b-8b71-6f9b5f58ed79" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6095939-f405-593b-8b71-6f9b5f58ed79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7a56aede-9c99-5d33-a79c-6c663e1f1ba1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-63214755-1ffa-5c0e-8b9c-4bdbd7a24af9" "answer-19fc9b9d-a070-5f24-acad-319ed34a70ed" "answer-ea7897ff-beb7-5588-8489-6f901a42a743" "answer-7a56aede-9c99-5d33-a79c-6c663e1f1ba1" "answer-eea5507f-9cf4-5f5d-a447-b31cf52084cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63214755-1ffa-5c0e-8b9c-4bdbd7a24af9" :answer/id #uuid "63214755-1ffa-5c0e-8b9c-4bdbd7a24af9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(Q∨P)∧¬R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19fc9b9d-a070-5f24-acad-319ed34a70ed" :answer/id #uuid "19fc9b9d-a070-5f24-acad-319ed34a70ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(¬Q∧¬P)∧¬R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea7897ff-beb7-5588-8489-6f901a42a743" :answer/id #uuid "ea7897ff-beb7-5588-8489-6f901a42a743" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(¬Q∧¬P)∨¬R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a56aede-9c99-5d33-a79c-6c663e1f1ba1" :answer/id #uuid "7a56aede-9c99-5d33-a79c-6c663e1f1ba1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(¬Q∨¬P)∧¬R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eea5507f-9cf4-5f5d-a447-b31cf52084cb" :answer/id #uuid "eea5507f-9cf4-5f5d-a447-b31cf52084cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬Q∨(P∧¬R)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f35f97f-518c-5bc3-8e7f-b4c49c35520a" :question/id #uuid "2f35f97f-518c-5bc3-8e7f-b4c49c35520a" :question/math-academy-id "q-1475" :question/problem "Simplify the statement  $¬(P∨¬Q)$ using De Morgan's laws." :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∧Q)≡¬P∨¬Q, \\\\ ¬(P∨Q)≡¬P∧¬Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∨¬Q) & ≡¬P∧¬(¬Q) \\\\  & ≡¬P∧Q\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f848964-4cd5-5959-b7fd-639dff393326"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f848964-4cd5-5959-b7fd-639dff393326" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f848964-4cd5-5959-b7fd-639dff393326" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5a65505b-4173-5672-96fb-eeb8f53e4fb7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6cdf4028-4812-5e3a-b1ca-c10dc61164a2" "answer-5a65505b-4173-5672-96fb-eeb8f53e4fb7" "answer-bc583e83-8045-599f-ad05-702e6de9d6ca" "answer-6bf40fe0-2946-5e5a-9e2a-be6004e4ca8b" "answer-6bc7205a-a182-5d64-b3b5-3a2807b547a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cdf4028-4812-5e3a-b1ca-c10dc61164a2" :answer/id #uuid "6cdf4028-4812-5e3a-b1ca-c10dc61164a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∧¬Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a65505b-4173-5672-96fb-eeb8f53e4fb7" :answer/id #uuid "5a65505b-4173-5672-96fb-eeb8f53e4fb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬P∧Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc583e83-8045-599f-ad05-702e6de9d6ca" :answer/id #uuid "bc583e83-8045-599f-ad05-702e6de9d6ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬P∧¬Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bf40fe0-2946-5e5a-9e2a-be6004e4ca8b" :answer/id #uuid "6bf40fe0-2946-5e5a-9e2a-be6004e4ca8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬P∨¬Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bc7205a-a182-5d64-b3b5-3a2807b547a8" :answer/id #uuid "6bc7205a-a182-5d64-b3b5-3a2807b547a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬Q∨¬P" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-97dcc406-82e2-57c8-880f-2a83c1dc8205" :question/id #uuid "97dcc406-82e2-57c8-880f-2a83c1dc8205" :question/math-academy-id "q-129826" :question/problem "Rewrite the statement $¬(¬A∧(¬B∨A))$ using De Morgan's laws." :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(A∨B)≡¬A∧¬B, \\\\ ¬(A∧B)≡¬A∨¬B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(¬A∧(¬B∨A)) & ≡¬(¬A)∨¬(¬B∨A) \\\\  & ≡A∨(¬(¬B)∧¬A) \\\\  & ≡A∨(B∧¬A)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-97779c75-c871-5f40-b22d-2c3c6f521f04"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-97779c75-c871-5f40-b22d-2c3c6f521f04" :answer-field/id #uuid "97779c75-c871-5f40-b22d-2c3c6f521f04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a3bad151-32df-5b30-89f4-1df23fa95050" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9422bec2-4a9a-5902-967d-1bee95d76f81" "answer-b278173e-938b-5dc8-9856-44dc092025a3" "answer-cdee5e32-593f-5078-9ffd-bdd90283badb" "answer-a3bad151-32df-5b30-89f4-1df23fa95050" "answer-02330894-f5f7-5da1-b7b2-e4aecffb6072"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9422bec2-4a9a-5902-967d-1bee95d76f81" :answer/id #uuid "9422bec2-4a9a-5902-967d-1bee95d76f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A∧(B∧¬A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b278173e-938b-5dc8-9856-44dc092025a3" :answer/id #uuid "b278173e-938b-5dc8-9856-44dc092025a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A∧(B∨A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdee5e32-593f-5078-9ffd-bdd90283badb" :answer/id #uuid "cdee5e32-593f-5078-9ffd-bdd90283badb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A∧(B∨¬A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3bad151-32df-5b30-89f4-1df23fa95050" :answer/id #uuid "a3bad151-32df-5b30-89f4-1df23fa95050" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A∨(B∧¬A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02330894-f5f7-5da1-b7b2-e4aecffb6072" :answer/id #uuid "02330894-f5f7-5da1-b7b2-e4aecffb6072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A∨(B∨¬A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060982 :tutorial/content "**De Morgan's laws** for logic tell us how to distribute a negation over a conjunction or disjunction.\n\n- De Morgan's law for conjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg ( A \\land B) \\equiv \\neg A \\lor \\neg B.\n$$\n\n- De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg ( A \\lor B) \\equiv \\neg A \\land \\neg B.\n$$\n\nIntuitively, you can think that the negation \"flips\" the conjunction into a disjunction, and vice versa.\n\nTo prove that these laws hold, we can construct truth tables:\n\n- The following truth table shows that $\\neg ( A \\land B) \\equiv \\neg A \\lor \\neg B{:}$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg ( A \\land B) \\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\lor \\neg B \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n\n- The following truth table shows that $\\neg ( A \\lor B) \\equiv \\neg A \\land \\neg B{:}$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg ( A \\lor B) \\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\land \\neg B \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059911 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "activity-9685461e-590c-5180-af3f-1791a8f4a4f3" :activity/id #uuid "9685461e-590c-5180-af3f-1791a8f4a4f3" :activity/title "Solving Systems of ODEs Using Variation of Parameters" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050355 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-5246a3a6-57b1-5c25-9b35-d0dbc9caa0dd" "step-c56298de-6a4a-5225-acfe-e2745c853056" "step-344d440c-ee63-5ff5-80e9-b7e2cf73c5b5" "step-058401a8-73fa-5425-9842-84a991542c1f" "step-1affbc8d-3508-571b-b687-c3b22e932e50"] :activity/first-step "step-5246a3a6-57b1-5c25-9b35-d0dbc9caa0dd" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5246a3a6-57b1-5c25-9b35-d0dbc9caa0dd" :step/id #uuid "5246a3a6-57b1-5c25-9b35-d0dbc9caa0dd" :step/content 17592186167175 :step/next "step-c56298de-6a4a-5225-acfe-e2745c853056" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c56298de-6a4a-5225-acfe-e2745c853056" :step/id #uuid "c56298de-6a4a-5225-acfe-e2745c853056" :step/content 17592186311737 :step/next "step-344d440c-ee63-5ff5-80e9-b7e2cf73c5b5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-344d440c-ee63-5ff5-80e9-b7e2cf73c5b5" :step/id #uuid "344d440c-ee63-5ff5-80e9-b7e2cf73c5b5" :step/content 17592186483355 :step/next "step-058401a8-73fa-5425-9842-84a991542c1f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-058401a8-73fa-5425-9842-84a991542c1f" :step/id #uuid "058401a8-73fa-5425-9842-84a991542c1f" :step/content 17592186497352 :step/next "step-1affbc8d-3508-571b-b687-c3b22e932e50" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1affbc8d-3508-571b-b687-c3b22e932e50" :step/id #uuid "1affbc8d-3508-571b-b687-c3b22e932e50" :step/content 17592186311830 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119843 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-023dfa42-4e6d-5f3b-a244-3651fae43041" "question-6d98c7f4-5b71-5445-b0c2-3ae12d58e232"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-023dfa42-4e6d-5f3b-a244-3651fae43041" :question/id #uuid "023dfa42-4e6d-5f3b-a244-3651fae43041" :question/math-academy-id "q-77483" :question/problem "$\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}=$" :question/worked-solution "The $1$rst row of the matrix contains two zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+3\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a6d6f5ed-1f32-5f94-b5db-36d00dc864a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a6d6f5ed-1f32-5f94-b5db-36d00dc864a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d6f5ed-1f32-5f94-b5db-36d00dc864a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fd5277a8-141f-53e6-a9f7-9f4b7a7bbabe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1f49c0ca-265e-5df5-adbc-18aec6bdbb48" "answer-485afcd0-3428-5eb2-9e7e-8703c4559a84" "answer-6e35f3f0-2c2c-5839-8102-0d9913bb5c81" "answer-fd5277a8-141f-53e6-a9f7-9f4b7a7bbabe" "answer-a152ae4b-8e59-51b4-8d21-56074bb83e2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f49c0ca-265e-5df5-adbc-18aec6bdbb48" :answer/id #uuid "1f49c0ca-265e-5df5-adbc-18aec6bdbb48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-485afcd0-3428-5eb2-9e7e-8703c4559a84" :answer/id #uuid "485afcd0-3428-5eb2-9e7e-8703c4559a84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e35f3f0-2c2c-5839-8102-0d9913bb5c81" :answer/id #uuid "6e35f3f0-2c2c-5839-8102-0d9913bb5c81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd5277a8-141f-53e6-a9f7-9f4b7a7bbabe" :answer/id #uuid "fd5277a8-141f-53e6-a9f7-9f4b7a7bbabe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a152ae4b-8e59-51b4-8d21-56074bb83e2d" :answer/id #uuid "a152ae4b-8e59-51b4-8d21-56074bb83e2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d98c7f4-5b71-5445-b0c2-3ae12d58e232" :question/id #uuid "6d98c7f4-5b71-5445-b0c2-3ae12d58e232" :question/math-academy-id "q-130016" :question/problem "$\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}=$" :question/worked-solution "The $1$st row of the matrix contains two zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix} & =5\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-2)\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-550a9655-a073-50b6-8445-5ed8af5e03e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-550a9655-a073-50b6-8445-5ed8af5e03e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "550a9655-a073-50b6-8445-5ed8af5e03e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e71c7726-37eb-5979-a6c4-384dbf9ee041" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec637a7a-cbc9-5a0e-a24b-8f0b7c1eaf0e" "answer-f6fbf5a2-cccc-5ad4-af62-850ce08f1201" "answer-e71c7726-37eb-5979-a6c4-384dbf9ee041" "answer-6f6902c6-be7e-52e4-a198-0504abe0a606" "answer-e5e48b02-3e81-5c81-b09e-e230a9386de9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec637a7a-cbc9-5a0e-a24b-8f0b7c1eaf0e" :answer/id #uuid "ec637a7a-cbc9-5a0e-a24b-8f0b7c1eaf0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}-5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6fbf5a2-cccc-5ad4-af62-850ce08f1201" :answer/id #uuid "f6fbf5a2-cccc-5ad4-af62-850ce08f1201" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e71c7726-37eb-5979-a6c4-384dbf9ee041" :answer/id #uuid "e71c7726-37eb-5979-a6c4-384dbf9ee041" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f6902c6-be7e-52e4-a198-0504abe0a606" :answer/id #uuid "6f6902c6-be7e-52e4-a198-0504abe0a606" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5e48b02-3e81-5c81-b09e-e230a9386de9" :answer/id #uuid "e5e48b02-3e81-5c81-b09e-e230a9386de9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119773 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fdf6e88c-e01c-539c-b77e-5f96909fea1b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fdf6e88c-e01c-539c-b77e-5f96909fea1b" :question/id #uuid "fdf6e88c-e01c-539c-b77e-5f96909fea1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130046" :question/problem "Calculate\n$\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "The $3$rd row of the matrix contains two zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\cdot {C}_{31}+2\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{33}+0\\cdot {C}_{34} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+5\\cdot {C}_{33} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+5\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+5\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1-4)+5(6-3) \\\\  & =-3+15 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+2\\cdot {C}_{22}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(5+4)+(0-2) \\\\  & =18-2 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot 12-2\\cdot 16=-20.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d329cca5-c5d9-5817-8c32-2b7df8e1d97f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d329cca5-c5d9-5817-8c32-2b7df8e1d97f" :answer-field/id #uuid "d329cca5-c5d9-5817-8c32-2b7df8e1d97f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answe